# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The MCP server list itself lives in ``openclaw.json``, not in the container environment."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le Baile Cúnta imscaradh, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP den chonradh ardán mar chliant insruthaithe-HTTP inmheánach le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Tá an liosta freastalaí MCP féin ina chónaí i ``openclaw.json``, ní sa timpeallacht coimeádán."

# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With Home Assistant deployed, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The MCP server list itself lives in `openclaw.json`, not in the container environment."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le Baile Cúnta imscaradh, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP den chonradh ardán mar chliant insruthaithe-HTTP inmheánach le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Tá an liosta freastalaí MCP féin ina chónaí i `openclaw.json`, ní sa timpeallacht coimeádán."

# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` registry under an `infinito:` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider's declared allowlist. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` plus an `HTTP_DENY_LIST` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
msgstr "**MCP conradh cliant:** Le freastalaí MCP imscaradh taobh leis, dearbhaíonn an ról an taobh cliant MCP an chonartha ardán mar chliant inmheánach sruthú-HTTP le polasaí uirlis léamh-amháin. Na cláir imscaradh gach soláthraí fuair sé amach sa chás-leibhéal `/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers` clárlann faoi `infinito:` ainm, siopaí an settings mar criptithe `CUSTOM_HEADERS` `authConfig`, údaraíonn gach iontráil agus cuireann sé i gcomparáid leis na huirlisí a fuair sé amach i gcoinne an tsoláthróra ar dhearbhaigh an cheadúliosta. `CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse` bioráin an imscaradh chuig freastalaithe MCP URL-bhunaithe, mar sin ní féidir aon sreabhadh sceite ordú stdio áitiúil. Reaching freastalaí MCP a réitíonn a URL taobh istigh den líonra coimeádán éilíonn `HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false` móide `HTTP_DENY_LIST` go gcoinníonn lúb siar agus na seoltaí scamall-metadata dhiúltú; araon a dhéantar ach amháin nuair a freastalaithe MCP aimsithe, agus go gcruthóidh an imscaradh go bhfuil an liosta beo ag cur in iúl iontráil throwaway ag gach seoladh dhiúltú. Iarrann fixture One bainistiú Agentflow uirlis ainmnithe amháin le hargóintí seasta agus tá sé chun báis ar gach imscaradh. Roinnt soláthraí isteach i sreabhadh de do chuid féin tréimhsí céim oibreoir."

# libretranslate
msgid "**MCP client contract:** With an MCP server deployed alongside it, the role declares the MCP client side of the platform contract as an internal streamable-HTTP client with a read-only tool policy. The deploy registers every discovered provider in the instance-level ``/api/v1/custom-mcp-servers`` registry under an ``infinito:`` name, stores the bearer as an encrypted ``CUSTOM_HEADERS`` ``authConfig``, authorizes each entry and compares the discovered tools against the provider’s declared allowlist. ``CUSTOM_MCP_PROTOCOL=sse`` pins the deployment to URL-based MCP servers, so no flow can spawn a local stdio command. Reaching an MCP server whose URL resolves inside the container network requires ``HTTP_SECURITY_CHECK=false`` plus an ``HTTP_DENY_LIST`` that keeps loopback and the cloud-metadata addresses denied; both are rendered only while MCP servers are discovered, and the deploy proves the list is live by pointing a throwaway entry at each denied address. One managed Agentflow fixture calls a single named tool with fixed arguments and is executed on every deploy. Wiring a provider into a flow of your own stays an operator step."
