msgid "**joomla local-login fallback spec** — `test-oidc-fallback.js:52` (the `?fallback=local` emergency hatch: local Joomla admin form login must reach the control panel). Root cause UNCONFIRMED. It is independent of the fixed OIDC-login spec: the fallback path short-circuits before the plugin's server-side discovery, so the committed `extra_hosts` fix does not cover it. The `secure => true` sticky-cookie hypothesis was rejected (`.onion` is a potentially-trustworthy origin and the e2e Firefox sets `dom.securecontext.allowlist_onions`, so Secure cookies are accepted over plain-http onion). Next step when it fails again post-fix: isolate the post-submit URL — Keycloak redirect (cookie lost) vs. form reject vs. slow control-panel render."
msgstr "**ghrian nochtadh: leath-scáth** — — — — `test-oidc-fallback.js:52` (an `?fallback=local` haiste éigeandála: ní mór logáil isteach foirm áitiúil Joomla admin teacht ar an bpainéal rialú). Fréamh faoi deara UNCONFIRMED. Tá sé neamhspleách ar an spec OIDC-login seasta: an cosán fallback gearr-ciorcaid roimh an breiseán ar fhreastalaí-taobh fionnachtain, mar sin an tiomanta `extra_hosts` Ní shocrú chlúdach. An bhfuil `secure => true` diúltaíodh hipitéis greamaitheach (`.onion` tionscnamh a d'fhéadfadh a bheith iontaofa agus an e2Leagann Firefox `dom.securecontext.allowlist_onions`, mar sin Glactar le fianáin Secure thar oinniún plain-http). An chéad chéim eile nuair a theipeann air arís iar-shocrú: leithlisiú an URL iar-ionad — Keycloak atreorú (fianán caillte) vs fhoirm dhiúltú vs. rialú-panel mall a dhéanamh."

