# libretranslate
msgid "A `Dockerfile.j2` with **Jinja2 control-flow logic** emits a **warning only**. The warning signals that the file should be reviewed to see whether the logic can be eliminated and the file migrated."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas `Dockerfile.j2` le **Déan teagmháil linn2 loighic rialaithe-sreabhadh** astaíonn **rabhadh amháin**. Na comharthaí rabhaidh gur chóir an comhad a athbhreithniú a fheiceáil an féidir an loighic a dhíchur agus an comhad a aistriú."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `Dockerfile.j2` with **no Jinja2 control-flow logic** causes a **test failure**. It MUST be migrated to `files/Dockerfile` with `ARG` declarations."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas `Dockerfile.j2` le **Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil2 loighic rialaithe-sreabhadh** cúiseanna **minicíocht uisce: flúirseach**. MUST sé a aistriú chuig `files/Dockerfile` le `ARG` dearbhuithe."

# libretranslate
msgid "A `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` variable defined in inventory, group vars, or host vars. No such file ships with the project. This form is an escape hatch for site-specific overrides."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` athróg sainmhínithe i fardal, vars grúpa, nó vars óstach. Níl aon longa comhad den sórt sin leis an tionscadal. Is é seo an fhoirm haiste éalú le haghaidh overrides suíomh-sonrach."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``database = '*'`` row dumps a whole instance with ``pg_dumpall``. It goes back through ``baudolo-restore cluster`` with the instance's superuser; its ``\\connect`` lines name the databases, while the consumers sit in the compose project of the engine, so both are checked."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas ``database = '*'`` dumpáil a chéile mar shampla iomlán le ``pg_dumpall``. Téann sé ar ais tríd ``baudolo-restore cluster`` leis an cás superuser; a ``\\connect`` línte ainm na bunachair shonraí, cé go suífidh na tomhaltóirí i dtionscadal an t-inneall, mar sin déantar an dá cheann a sheiceáil."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``host_gateway`` upstream resolves through ``host.docker.internal`` in ``/etc/hosts`` (host gateway), which the request-time ``resolver`` cannot see, so it renders as a literal directive like compose."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas ``host_gateway`` réiteach sruth tríd ``host.docker.internal`` i ``/etc/hosts`` (geata óstach), cé acu an t-iarratas ``resolver`` Ní féidir a fheiceáil, mar sin déanann sé mar threoir litriúil cosúil le chumadh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``maxmemory`` ceiling derived from the service ``mem_limit`` with an ``allkeys-lru`` policy."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas ``maxmemory`` uasteorainn a dhíorthaítear ón tseirbhís ``mem_limit`` le ``allkeys-lru`` beartas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``mount --make-rshared /`` runs once in the deploy container before the runner starts, because MDAD’s systemd units bind-mount ``/matrix/synapse/storage`` with ``bind-propagation=slave``, which requires shared/slave propagation on the source."
msgstr "Amharc ar gach eolas ``mount --make-rshared /`` Ritheann uair amháin sa choimeádán imscaradh sula dtosaíonn an dara háit, mar gheall ar aonaid córasaithe MDAD ceangal-mount ``/matrix/synapse/storage`` le ``bind-propagation=slave``, a éilíonn iomadú roinnte / daor ar an bhfoinse."

# libretranslate
msgid "A ``svc-bkp-*`` pre-backup hook for ``bench backup`` is NOT wired in v1 (deferred to a follow-up requirement). The v1 backup story relies on the standard ``svc-bkp-*`` driver picking up the central MariaDB DB and the role’s named volumes. To make a Frappe-aware snapshot in flight, run:"
