# libretranslate
msgid "A blank ``current`` (the addon tracks the app default) never produces a suggestion, and a non-semver ``latest`` is ignored so the checker never proposes a non-comparable tag."
msgstr "A bán ``current`` (an addon rianta an réamhshocraithe app) riamh Táirgeann moladh, agus neamh-semver ``latest`` neamhaird mar sin ní mhol an seiceálaí chlib neamh-comparable."

# libretranslate
msgid "A block device (remote path under ``/dev/``) is recovered on the host over ssh (the host must carry the repo checkout), then the restored backup tree is rsync-pulled. An image file is rsync-pulled and recovered locally. Either way the result is a local backup root the caller then recovers from."
msgstr "gléas bloc (cosán iargúlta faoi ``/dev/``) aisghabháil ar an óstach thar ssh (ní mór don óstach a dhéanamh ar an repo checkout), ansin tá an crann cúltaca ar ais rsync-pulled. Tá comhad íomhá rsync-pulled agus aisghabháil go háitiúil. Ceachtar slí go bhfuil an toradh ar fhréamh cúltaca áitiúil an callaire recovers ansin ó."

# libretranslate
msgid "A block naming a key the entity does not carry, or a type the resolver does not know, would otherwise pin nothing and say nothing."
msgstr "A bloc ainmniú eochair nach bhfuil an t-eintiteas a iompar, nó cineál nach bhfuil a fhios ag an réiteoir, bheadh bioráin ar shlí eile rud ar bith agus a rá rud ar bith."

# libretranslate
msgid "A block that only one side has is usually a feature the other never had. Check whether it was superseded before dropping it — grep for its variables."
msgstr "Tá bloc go bhfuil ach taobh amháin de ghnáth gné an ceann eile riamh a bhí. Seiceáil an raibh sé in áit roimh dropping sé - grep le haghaidh a athróg."

# libretranslate
msgid "A body that asserts only constants (`expect(1).toBe(1)`) without driving any role surface is rejected on review."
msgstr "A comhlacht a dhearbhaíonn ach tairiseachs (`expect(1).toBe(1)`) gan tiomáint aon dromchla ról diúltaíodh ar athbhreithniú."

# libretranslate
msgid "A body that carries a `TODO`, `STUB`, `FIXME`, or `XXX` marker is rejected. The contract requires real flows, not deferred work."
msgstr "A comhlacht a iompraíonn `TODO`, `STUB`, `FIXME`, nó `XXX` Tá marcóir diúltaíodh. Éilíonn an conradh sreabhadh fíor, ní obair iarchurtha."

# libretranslate
msgid "A body that contains only `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(...)` (or any combination of helper calls) without at least one `expect(...)`, `await <fn>(...)`, or equivalent real-flow step is rejected."
msgstr "Comhlacht go bhfuil ach `skipUnlessServiceEnabled(...)` (nó aon teaglaim de ghlaonna cúntóir) gan ceann amháin ar a laghad `expect(...)`, `await <fn>(...)`, nó céim fíor-sreabhadh coibhéiseach diúltaíodh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A branch is ready to be opened as a pull request"
msgstr "Tá brainse réidh le hoscailt mar iarratas tarraingthe"

# libretranslate
msgid "A bridged service block MUST carry the standard `enabled` / `shared` flags so requirement 019 (services.yml parity) and the SSO/LDAP coverage requirements (017, 018) continue to apply unchanged."
msgstr "A bloc seirbhíse droichead MUST dhéanamh ar an gcaighdeán `enabled` / Baile `shared` bratacha riachtanas sin 019 (services.yml parity) agus riachtanais clúdach SSO/LDAP (017, 018) leanúint ar aghaidh ag cur isteach gan athrú."

# libretranslate
msgid "A built-in (embedded) runner executes tasks in the main container; external `semaphore runner` agents are optional for scale-out."
msgstr "A tógadh isteach (leabaithe leabaithe) rádala fhorghníomhú tascanna sa phríomh-choimeádán; seachtrach `semaphore runner` Tá gníomhairí roghnach le haghaidh scála amach."

# libretranslate
msgid "A built-in ``rabbitmq-diagnostics ping`` healthcheck."
msgstr "A tógadh isteach ``rabbitmq-diagnostics ping`` seiceáil sláinte."

# libretranslate
msgid "A built-in `rabbitmq-diagnostics ping` healthcheck."
msgstr "A tógadh isteach `rabbitmq-diagnostics ping` seiceáil sláinte."

# libretranslate
msgid "A bulleted list of the most important capabilities. Each item MUST start with a **bold** label followed by a colon and a short explanation."
msgstr "Liosta feasach de na cumais is tábhachtaí. Gach mír MUST tús a chur le **trom trom trom** lipéad ina dhiaidh sin colon agus míniú gearr."

# libretranslate
msgid "A candidate the curated relevance rules reject is silently dropped so broad marketplaces never produce unreviewable noise."
msgstr "Tá iarrthóir na rialacha ábharthachta leasaithe dhiúltú thit go ciúin mar sin margaí leathan riamh a tháirgeadh torann neamh-athbhreithnithe."

# libretranslate
msgid "A change is incompatible with prior inventories, on-disk role-meta layout, deploy CLI, or stored runtime state."
msgstr "Tá athrú ar neamhréir le fardail roimh ré, ar-disk ról-treoir leagan amach, imscaradh CLI, nó a stóráil stáit runtime."

# libretranslate
msgid "A changed source keeps its previous translation as a fuzzy entry, a removed source disappears."
msgstr "Coinníonn foinse athraithe a aistriúchán roimhe seo mar iontráil fuzzy, imíonn foinse a bhaint."

# libretranslate
msgid "A classic personal access token MAY be used as a fallback for unrelated automation, but it MUST NOT be used here because user-bound credentials expand the blast radius and require manual rotation."
msgstr "A MAY rochtain phearsanta clasaiceach a úsáid mar fallback le haghaidh uathoibriú neamhghaolmhar, ach NÍ MÓR é a úsáid anseo toisc go bhfuil dintiúir úsáideora-cheangal leathnú an ga soinneáin agus a cheangal ar rothlú láimhe."

# libretranslate
msgid "A clean `down && up` is required after the change: `make compose-up` alone recreates the bridge but compose then re-attaches existing containers with dynamic IPs instead of the static `default.env` ones, which breaks CoreDNS."
msgstr "glan `down && up` ag teastáil tar éis an athraithe: `make compose-up` ina n-aonar recreates an droichead ach a chumadh ansin ath-ionsaithe coimeádáin atá ann cheana féin le IP dinimiciúil in ionad an statach `default.env` cinn, a bhriseann CoreDNS."

# libretranslate
msgid "A client MUST NOT treat an unreachable provider as fatal while the play is still running. Roles deploy in dependency order, so a client that probes during its own role can run before a provider exists at all, and aborting there prevents that provider from ever deploying. This is the same exemption `credential_missing` already carries, and it ends the same way: the reconciliation stage probes with `MCP_RECONCILE_STRICT` once every provider has run, and a provider still unreachable there is a real failure."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR cliant a chóireáil soláthraí unreachable mar marfach cé go bhfuil an spraoi ag rith fós. Róil imscaradh in ord dependency, mar sin is féidir le cliant a probes le linn a ról féin a reáchtáil sula bhfuil soláthraí ar chor ar bith, agus aborting ann cosc a chur ar an soláthraí ó riamh imscaradh. Is é seo an díolúine chéanna `credential_missing` cheana féin, agus críochnaíonn sé ar an mbealach céanna: an chéim athmhuintearais probes le `MCP_RECONCILE_STRICT` uair amháin tá gach soláthraí reáchtáil, agus soláthraí fós unreachable tá teip fíor."

# libretranslate
msgid "A client declares what it can present instead of what it serves:"
msgstr "Dearbhaíonn cliant cad is féidir é a chur i láthair in ionad an méid a fheidhmíonn sé:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A client role discovers enabled shared server roles through the lookup, resolves the per-server credential, then connects server-to-server to each `/mcp` endpoint over Streamable HTTP. No candidate list is hard-coded and no browser-side fetch is involved."
msgstr "Faigheann ról cliant ar chumas róil freastalaí roinnte tríd an lookup, réitíonn an chreidiúnacht in aghaidh an-freastalaí, ansin nascann freastalaí-le-freastalaí le gach `/mcp` endpoint thar HTTP Streamable. Níl aon liosta iarrthóir crua-chódaithe agus níl aon bhrabhsálaí-taobh fetch gceist."

# libretranslate
msgid "A client-only block MUST NOT declare an `endpoint`."
msgstr "A cliant-amháin bloc NACH dhearbhú `endpoint`."

# libretranslate
msgid "A cluster row states the cluster marker where a single-database row names a database, so :func:`credentials_of` would file every instance under the same key and keep only the first. Cluster credentials are therefore keyed by instance."
msgstr "Deir sraith braisle an marcóir braisle ina n-ainmneacha sraith aon-sonraí bunachar sonraí, mar sin :func:`credentials_of` Bheadh comhad gach cás faoin eochair céanna agus a choinneáil ach an chéad. Tá dintiúir braistear dá bhrí sin eochairithe ag shampla."

# libretranslate
msgid "A colon suffix on `<source>` is classified by shape:"
msgstr "A iarmhír colon ar `<source>` Tá rangaithe de réir cruth:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A complete digital learning environment for schools, academies, and universities."
msgstr "Timpeallacht foghlama digiteach iomlán do scoileanna, acadaimh, agus ollscoileanna."

# libretranslate
msgid "A computed fallback defined in `_compute(short_key, resolved, variables)`."
msgstr "Aiseolas ríomhairithe sainithe i `_compute(short_key, resolved, variables)`."

# libretranslate
msgid "A concrete end-to-end illustration of how the pieces compose. Nothing here is a new mechanism; it maps onto the decisions above."
msgstr "Léiríonn deireadh-le-deireadh coincréite ar an gcaoi a chumtar na píosaí. Ní dhéanfaidh aon ní anseo meicníocht nua; léarscáileanna sé ar na cinntí thuas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A condition that makes the replay unprovable."
msgstr "coinníoll a dhéanann an replay unprovable."

# libretranslate
msgid "A confirmed hit is cached on disk. The probe stays on the upstream registry: it exists to prove the declared pin is still pullable from where the deploy pulls it, which a mirrored copy cannot answer for."
msgstr "Tá hit deimhnithe i dtaisce ar diosca. Fanann an probe ar an gclárú réamhtheachtach: tá sé ann a chruthú go bhfuil an bioráin dearbhaithe in-aibithe fós ó áit a tharraingíonn an t-imscaradh é, nach féidir le cóip scáthaithe a fhreagairt."

# libretranslate
msgid "A constant hides the role id the substring rule looks for, so every SPOT of this kind MUST be listed here or the roles referencing it silently drop their provider from the static closure."
msgstr "Tá seithí leanúnach an ról id an riail substring Breathnaíonn, mar sin gach nóta den chineál seo MUST a liostú anseo nó na róil tagairt sé go ciúin titim a soláthraí as an dúnadh statach."

# libretranslate
msgid "A consumer is a deployed role whose merged config enables a shared database of the provider's engine; a role with a dedicated database brings its own volume and is no consumer of the provider. A provider without a consumer holds only the databases its engine creates for itself, so no databases.csv row names it and baudolo records its volume undumped."
msgstr "Is tomhaltóir ról imscaradh a chumasc config bunachar sonraí roinnte ar inneall an tsoláthraí; ról le bunachar sonraí tiomnaithe Tugann a thoirt féin agus nach bhfuil aon tomhaltóir ar an soláthraí. Tá soláthraí gan tomhaltóir ach na bunachair shonraí a chruthaíonn a inneall dó féin, mar sin níl aon databases.csv ainmneacha a chéile é agus baudolo taifid a toirt míchuí."

# libretranslate
msgid "A consumer user named `<entity>` is restricted to keys matching `<entity>:*`."
msgstr "úsáideoir tomhaltóra ainmnithe `<entity>` srianta do mheaitseáil eochracha `<entity>:*`."

# libretranslate
msgid "A consuming role MAY override a shared service's config field in its own ``meta/services.yml`` ``services.<key>`` block. When it does not, the value falls back to the *provider* role's native declaration — the role whose entity name is ``<key>`` (e.g. ``svc-net-tor`` for ``tor``). This keeps provider defaults (e.g. ``tor.exclusive`` / ``tor.primary``) in one place while every consumer stays free to override the field per app."
msgstr "Ról Tógann MAY override seirbhís roinnte réimse config ina féin ``meta/services.yml`` ``services.<key>`` bloc. Nuair nach ndéanann sé, titeann an luach ar ais go dtí an *soláthróir* dearbhú dúchais an róil — an ról a bhfuil a ainm eintitis ``<key>`` (e.g. ``svc-net-tor`` le haghaidh ``tor``). Coinníonn sé seo mainneachtainí soláthraí (e.g. ``tor.exclusive`` / Baile ``tor.primary``) in áit amháin nuair a fhanann gach tomhaltóir saor in aisce a shárú ar an réimse in aghaidh an app."

# libretranslate
msgid "A container resolves through the runtime's embedded server on 127.0.0.11, which forwards to whatever the network was created with, so ``inspect`` on the container shows the address but never the forwarder behind it."
msgstr "Réitíonn coimeádán tríd an bhfreastalaí leabaithe runtime ar 127.0.0.11, a ar aghaidh go dtí cuma cad a cruthaíodh an líonra le, mar sin ``inspect`` ar an gcoimeádán léiríonn an seoladh ach ní an seoltóir taobh thiar de."

# libretranslate
msgid "A content publishing and distribution ecosystem for creators and media organizations."
msgstr "A ábhar a fhoilsiú agus a dháileadh éiceachóras do creators agus eagraíochtaí meáin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A cyber-resilient sovereign infrastructure foundation for high-assurance environments."
msgstr "Bunús bonneagair ceannasach cíbear-friotaí do thimpeallachtaí ard-árachas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A declaration names exactly one probe and any number of prefixes, either as one string or as a list. This module owns that grammar: the aliases, the validation and the timing arithmetic that decides what a composed probe inherits."
msgstr "Ainmníonn dearbhú go díreach probe amháin agus aon líon na réimeanna, mar aon teaghrán nó mar liosta. Is leis an modúl seo go gramadach: na ailiases, an bailíochtú agus an uimhríocht uainiú a chinneann cad a hoidhreacht probe comhdhéanta."

# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "A declared value that is a ``{start, end}`` mapping renders as ``start-end`` on both sides, so a relay range needs no special term."
msgstr "Luach dearbhaithe is ea ``{start, end}`` rindreáil mapála mar ``start-end`` ar an dá thaobh, mar sin ní mór raon sealaíochta aon téarma speisialta."

# libretranslate
msgid "A dedicated disk mounted straight onto `/var/lib/docker` needs no special layout: baudolo carves its snapshot **inside** the subject, as `<data root>/.baudolo-<tag>`, so source and destination are always on the same filesystem. Placing it beside the subject would fail with `EXDEV` exactly on that layout, since the parent directory then belongs to a different filesystem."
msgstr "A diosca tiomnaithe suite díreach isteach `/var/lib/docker` riachtanais aon leagan amach speisialta: carves baudolo a snapshot **taobh istigh** an t-ábhar, mar `<data root>/.baudolo-<tag>`, mar sin tá foinse agus ceann scríbe i gcónaí ar an gcóras comhad céanna. Bheadh chur in aice leis an ábhar theipeann le `EXDEV` go díreach ar an leagan amach, ós rud é go mbaineann an eolaire tuismitheoir ansin le córas comhaid éagsúla."

# libretranslate
msgid "A dedicated disk mounted straight onto ``/var/lib/docker`` needs no special layout: baudolo carves its snapshot **inside** the subject, as ``<data root>/.baudolo-<tag>``, so source and destination are always on the same filesystem. Placing it beside the subject would fail with ``EXDEV`` exactly on that layout, since the parent directory then belongs to a different filesystem."
msgstr "A diosca tiomnaithe suite díreach isteach ``/var/lib/docker`` riachtanais aon leagan amach speisialta: carves baudolo a snapshot **taobh istigh** an t-ábhar, mar ``<data root>/.baudolo-<tag>``, mar sin tá foinse agus ceann scríbe i gcónaí ar an gcóras comhad céanna. Bheadh chur in aice leis an ábhar theipeann le ``EXDEV`` go díreach ar an leagan amach, ós rud é go mbaineann an eolaire tuismitheoir ansin le córas comhaid éagsúla."

# libretranslate
msgid "A deploy job is titled ``<mode glyph><tor glyph><distro glyph><filesystem glyph><architecture glyph><display name> <variant>`` with an optional trailing ⭐ for a priority row. The middle is resolved through the display-name codec rather than matched as a raw role id: job names carry display names, so a regex over ``web-app-…`` silently matched nothing and every failure went unreported."
msgstr "Tá post imscaradh dar teideal ``<mode glyph><tor glyph><distro glyph><filesystem glyph><architecture glyph><display name> <variant>`` le rianaithe roghnach le haghaidh sraith tosaíochta. Tá an lár réiteach tríd an taispeáint-ainm codec seachas mheaitseáil mar ról amh id: ainmneacha poist a sheoladh ainmneacha taispeáint, mar sin regex thar ``web-app-…`` adh mheaitseáil rud ar bith agus gach teip chuaigh neamhthuairiscithe."

# libretranslate
msgid "A deploy job title carries the whole row it deployed -- role, variant, mode, onion state, distro, filesystem, architecture -- and :mod:`utils.github.variant.selection` is the grammar that writes it back down."
msgstr "Déanann teideal poist imscaradh an tsraith iomlán a imscaradh sé - ról, malairt, modh, stát oinniún, distro, córas comhaid, ailtireacht - agus :mod:`utils.github.variant.selection` Is é an gramadach a scríobhann sé ar ais síos."

# libretranslate
msgid "A deploy with zero or more than one manager fails at inventory-validation time, never at runtime."
msgstr "A imscaradh le nialas nó níos mó ná mar a theipeann bainisteoir amháin ag am fardal-luacháil, riamh ag runtime."

# libretranslate
msgid "A deployment that keeps the shipped `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` serves names under `infinito.localhost`. Those exist in no zone, so a task that reaches the deployment's own domain from the host depends on the `myhostname` NSS module, which maps any `*.localhost` name to loopback per RFC 6761."
msgstr "Imscaradh a choinníonn an long `DOMAIN_PRIMARY` freastal ar ainmneacha faoi `infinito.localhost`. Glacfar ann in aon chrios, mar sin de chúram a shroicheann an t-imscaradh bhfearann féin as an óstach ag brath ar an `myhostname` NSS modúl, a léarscáileanna aon `*.localhost` ainm ar ais in aghaidh RFC 6761."

# libretranslate
msgid "A deployment that keeps the shipped ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY`` serves names under ``infinito.localhost``. Those exist in no zone, so a task that reaches the deployment’s own domain from the host depends on the ``myhostname`` NSS module, which maps any ``*.localhost`` name to loopback per RFC 6761."
msgstr "Imscaradh a choinníonn an long ``DOMAIN_PRIMARY`` freastal ar ainmneacha faoi ``infinito.localhost``. Glacfar ann in aon chrios, mar sin de chúram a shroicheann an t-imscaradh bhfearann féin as an óstach ag brath ar an ``myhostname`` NSS modúl, a léarscáileanna aon ``*.localhost`` ainm ar ais in aghaidh RFC 6761."

# libretranslate
msgid "A detailed documentation for the use and administration of Nextcloud on Infinito.Nexus you will find [here](docs/README.md)."
msgstr "Doiciméid mhionsonraithe maidir le húsáid agus riaradh Nextcloud ar Infinito.Nexus gheobhaidh tú [anseo](docs/README.md)."

