msgstr "A blocker doiciméadaithe nuair is féidir aon cheann de na thuas a chaomhnú teorainn údaraithe an t-iarratas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A failing pre-state snapshot aborts the deploy (no `suppress_flush`): no update proceeds without a successful backup of the state it is about to change. `svc-bkp-local-2-device` is never started at deploy time (no device present); it stays plug-triggered via its `.mount` unit."
msgstr "A borts snapshot réamh-stáit an imscaradh (Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil `suppress_flush`): aon fáltais cothrom le dáta gan cúltaca rathúil ar an stát tá sé ar tí a athrú. `svc-bkp-local-2-device` riamh thosaigh ag am imscaradh (aon fheiste i láthair); Fanann sé plug-triggered tríd a `.mount` aonad."

# libretranslate
msgid "A failure whose root cause is container runtime state (config, plugin, user binding, env) is by definition reproducible-there and does NOT qualify for the post-deploy-state exception."
msgstr "Is é teip a bhfuil cúis fhréamh acu ná stát runtime coimeádáin (config, breiseán, úsáideoir ceangailteach, env) go bhfuil sé de réir sainmhíniú ath-inspreagtha agus NACH gcáilíonn don eisceacht iar-imlonnaithe-stáit."

# libretranslate
msgid "A fallback MUST stay inside the permitted set, and a run whose whole permitted set is unservable MUST fail rather than leave it. The job title and the artifact name carry the kind the matrix assigned; the step summary carries the effective one."
msgstr "A MUST fallback fanacht taobh istigh den tsraith ceadaithe, agus tá a reáchtáil a bhfuil sraith iomlán ceadaithe theipeann MUST unservable seachas é a fhágáil. Déanann an teideal poist agus an t-ainm Déantán an cineál maitrís sannta; déanann an achoimre chéim an ceann éifeachtach."

# libretranslate
msgid "A fallback is reported, never silent. The job title and artifact name carry the kind the matrix *assigned*, while [docker_dataroot.sh](../../scripts/tests/deploy/utils/filesystem/docker_dataroot.sh) writes the *effective* filesystem and the reason into the step summary. When a run has to prove a filesystem-dependent path, read the summary rather than the title, or name the kind on the run to make it a demand. The snapshot mode of `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` is the case that matters: it only engages on btrfs and zfs."
msgstr "Tuairiscítear fallback, riamh adh. An teideal poist agus ainm Déantán a dhéanamh ar an chineál an maitrís *sannta sannadh*, cé [docker_dataroot.sh](../../scripts/tests/deploy/utils/filesystem/docker_dataroot.sh) scríobhann an *éifeachtach* córas comhaid agus an chúis isteach ar an achoimre chéim. Nuair a reáchtáil a chruthú comhad córas-spleách cosán, léamh an achoimre seachas an teideal, nó ainm an cineál ar an rith a dhéanamh ar éileamh. An modh pictiúr de `svc-bkp-volume-2-local` Is é an cás go nithe: ní bhaineann sé ach le btrfs agus zfs."

# libretranslate
msgid "A federated and community-driven platform for discussion, media sharing, and social networking."
msgstr "A ardán chothaithe agus pobail-tiomáinte le haghaidh plé, a roinnt meáin, agus líonraithe sóisialta."

# libretranslate
msgid "A final `make compose-deploy mode=reinstall apps=<role> full_cycle=true` run has completed with the spec passing against the freshly provisioned stack. Inner-loop passes alone do NOT satisfy this gate."
msgstr "A final `make compose-deploy mode=reinstall apps=<role> full_cycle=true` reáchtáil curtha i gcrích leis an spec rith i gcoinne an chairn freshly ar fáil. Ní dhéanann Inner-loop pasanna ina n-aonar NACH shásamh an geata."

# libretranslate
msgid "A flag is ``true`` only when the addon is both ``enabled`` AND ``required``. Optional addons (``required: false``) are intentionally skipped by the spec suite — they are a variant axis, not a guaranteed surface — so their gate flag is ``false`` even when enabled."
msgstr "Tá bratach ``true`` ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an addon araon ``enabled`` agus ``required``. Breiseáin roghnacha (``required: false``) a skipped d'aon ghnó ag an seomra spec - tá siad ais athraitheach, ní dromchla ráthaithe - mar sin tá a n-brat geata ``false`` fiú nuair ar chumas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A fork PR triggers a `pull_request_target` run that builds and mirrors any new images needed by the fork, authenticating to GHCR with the per-job `GITHUB_TOKEN`."
msgstr "A forc PR triggers a `pull_request_target` reáchtáil a thógann agus scátháin aon íomhánna nua ag teastáil ag an forc, fhíordheimhniú go GHCR leis an in aghaidh an-post `GITHUB_TOKEN`."

# libretranslate
msgid "A fragment can only ever be stricter than the host already is. In nftables an ``accept`` terminates its own base chain and nothing more: the packet still traverses every other chain at that hook, and a ``drop`` in any of them wins. A rule that has to overrule a policy someone else set, such as the ``DROP`` docker installs on forwarded packets, does not belong in a fragment at all; it belongs in the chain that carries that policy."
msgstr "Ní féidir le ilroinnt a bheith níos déine ná an t-óstach cheana féin. I nftables an ``accept`` foirceannadh a slabhra bonn féin agus rud ar bith níos mó: an paicéad go fóill trasna gach slabhra eile ag an Hook, agus ``drop`` in aon cheann acu Bhuaigh. riail go bhfuil a overrule duine polasaí eile a leagtar, mar shampla an ``DROP`` docker installs ar paicéid ar aghaidh, nach mbaineann i blúirí ar chor ar bith; mbaineann sé sa slabhra a dhéanann an polasaí sin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A fragment can only ever be stricter than the host already is. In nftables an `accept` terminates its own base chain and nothing more: the packet still traverses every other chain at that hook, and a `drop` in any of them wins. A rule that has to overrule a policy someone else set, such as the `DROP` docker installs on forwarded packets, does not belong in a fragment at all; it belongs in the chain that carries that policy."
