msgstr "A post URL Cúngú an íoslódáil chuig an post app; a lom reáchtáil URL pulls gach `role-runtimes-*` Déantán sa reáchtáil."

# libretranslate
msgid "A job counts as failed when it never finished, when the module reported ``failed``, or when a command returned a non-zero ``rc``. What distinguishes a real failure from an idempotent no-op differs per API and lives in different keys: modules put it in ``msg`` (cloudflare answers \"An identical record already exists\"), commands put it in ``stdout`` (``ollama pull`` prints \"up to date\" and exits non-zero). Both are searched, so a caller passes the tolerated phrasing and does not have to know which key carries it."
msgstr "Comhaireamh post mar theip nuair riamh críochnaithe é, nuair a thuairiscigh an modúl ``failed``, nó nuair a d'fhill ordú neamh-zero ``rc``. Cad idirdhealú teip fíor ó idempotent aon-op difriúil in aghaidh an API agus ina chónaí i eochracha éagsúla: modúil a chur i ``msg`` (taiseachas aeir: fliuch \"Tá taifead comhionann ann cheana féin\"), orduithe a chur i ``stdout`` (``ollama pull`` priontaí \"suas go dtí dáta\" agus bealaí amach neamh-zero). Tá an dá chuardach, mar sin a théann glaoiteoir an frásaí fhulaingt agus nach bhfuil a fhios a bhfuil eochair ndéanann sé."

# libretranslate
msgid "A job title states its whole combination, which lets `--failed` replay the mode, onion state and distribution, and makes a plan table row comparable to the job it predicts."
msgstr "Deir teideal poist a meascán iomlán, a ligeann `--failed` replay an modh, stát oinniún agus dáileadh, agus a dhéanann sraith tábla plean inchomparáide leis an bpost tuartha sé."

# libretranslate
msgid "A job's green conclusion is **NOT** evidence for a specific change. Before citing a run as proof, you MUST locate the line in that job's log where the change executed: a Playwright spec's `✓` (a leading `-` means the spec was skipped), the env var inside the container, or the command text of an `if:`-gated step. If the string is absent, report the run as silent on the change, not as supporting it."
msgstr "Tá post ar chonclúid glas **Déan teagmháil linn** fianaise ar athrú sonrach. Sula lua reáchtáil mar chruthúnas, MUST tú a aimsiú ar an líne sa phost sin logáil i gcás an t-athrú fhorghníomhú: spec Playwright ar `✓` (le rá `-` Ciallaíonn go raibh skipped an spec), an var env taobh istigh den choimeádán, nó an téacs ordú ar `if:`-gated céim. Má tá an teaghrán as láthair, tuairisc a thabhairt ar an reáchtáil mar adh ar an athrú, ní mar thacaíocht dó."

# libretranslate
msgid "A key that some environment declares per run therefore MUST be written by a dedicated handler through `eb.set`. The exporting shell still wins for its own run, because [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) preserves non-empty caller values when it sources `.env`; the file keeps the derived default. `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB` and `INFINITO_CACHE_STACK` are written this way. Note the consequence: for those keys `.env` and the running shell can legitimately disagree, and `.env` is not the authority."
msgstr "A eochair go Dearbhaíonn roinnt timpeallacht in aghaidh a reáchtáil dá bhrí sin MUST a scríobh ag láimhseálaí tiomnaithe trí `eb.set`. Bhuaigh an bhlaosc onnmhairithe fós lena reáchtáil féin, mar gheall ar [load.sh](../../scripts/meta/env/load.sh) caomhnaíonn luachanna glaoiteora neamh-empty nuair a fhoinsíonn sé `.env`; Coinníonn an comhad an réamhshocraithe díorthaithe. `INFINITO_RUNNING_ON_GITHUB` agus `INFINITO_CACHE_STACK` scríofa ar an mbealach seo. Tabhair faoi deara an iarmhairt: do na heochracha `.env` agus is féidir leis an bhlaosc ag rith easaontas dlisteanach, agus `.env` nach é an t-údarás."

# libretranslate
msgid "A key's comment is the most recent contiguous block of `# ...` lines directly above the `KEY=...` line, joined with single spaces. Section headers (`# --- ... ---`) are treated as separators: they reset the pending comment so the next key starts fresh, instead of inheriting the heading line as its own documentation."
msgstr "Is é trácht eochair an bloc is déanaí contiguous de `# ...` línte díreach os cionn an `KEY=...` líne, ceangailte le spásanna aonair. Ceannairí na Roinne (`# --- ... ---`) cóireáilte mar deighilteoirí: athshocrú siad an trácht ar feitheamh mar sin tosaíonn an chéad eochair eile úr, in ionad oidhreacht an líne ceannteideal mar a doiciméadú féin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A label that silently stops resolving to arm64 turns the whole axis into a green lie."
msgstr "A lipéad a stopann go ciúin réiteach a lámh64 casadh an ais ar fad isteach i bréag glas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A lightweight, Docker-powered UI framework that offers Infinito.Nexus users a unified interface to access all their applications in one intuitive dashboard. 🚀"
msgstr "A lightweight, Docker-chumhachtaithe Chomhéadain creat a thairgeann Infinito.Nexus úsáideoirí comhéadan aontaithe chun rochtain a fháil ar gach a n-iarratas i Painéal na nIonstraimí iomasach amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A list of external links relevant to the software or the deployment. Link text MUST be a descriptive label or the domain name. Never use the full URL."
msgstr "Liosta de na naisc sheachtracha a bhaineann leis na bogearraí nó leis an imscaradh. Link téacs MUST bheith ina lipéad tuairisciúil nó an t-ainm fearainn. Ná bain úsáid as an URL iomlán."

# libretranslate
msgid "A literal ``shared: false`` (not a Jinja expression) is the role author pinning an engine the central provider cannot serve. Honouring it is only safe on a manager-pinned role, where the volume stays node-local and the sidecar carries the matching placement constraint."
msgstr "A litriúil ``shared: false`` (Ní léiriú Jinja) Is é an t-údar ról pinning inneall nach féidir leis an soláthraí lárnach freastal. Onórach go bhfuil sé ach sábháilte ar ról bainisteoir-bioráin, i gcás ina bhfanann an toirt nód-áitiúil agus déanann an sidecar an srian socrúcháin meaitseáil."

# libretranslate
msgid "A local deploy is failing on the host"
msgstr "Tá imscaradh áitiúil ag teip ar an óstach"

# libretranslate
msgid "A location not starting with ``/`` is a remote ``[user@]host:/path``."
msgstr "suíomh nach bhfuil ag tosú le ``/`` Is iargúlta ``[user@]host:/path``."

# libretranslate
msgid "A long-running worker (own image, gated on both endpoints present) that:"
msgstr "A oibrí fada ag rith (íomhá féin, gated ar an dá endpoints láthair) sin:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A malformed filter expression."
msgstr "A léiriú scagaire malformed."

# libretranslate
msgid "A manager-pinned role keeps its volumes node-local (``swarm_nfs_backed``) and its DB sidecar carries the matching placement constraint, so a literal ``shared: false`` there is honoured instead of overridden — Magento hard-fails ``setup:install`` on the central MariaDB major."
msgstr "Coinníonn ról bainisteoir-bioráin a méideanna nód-áitiúil (``swarm_nfs_backed``) agus déanann a sidecar DB an srian socrúcháin meaitseáil, mar sin litriúil ``shared: false`` tá onóir in ionad ró-mharcaíochta - Magento crua-fails ``setup:install`` ar an MariaDB lárnach mór."

# libretranslate
msgid "A mapping deep-merges, so naming one key changes that key and nothing else. ``null`` empties the topic, which is the only way to say \"bring nothing\": merged, an empty mapping is a no-op and would leave exactly the services the round was trying to shed."
msgstr "A mapáil domhain-cumasc, mar sin ainmniú athruithe eochair amháin go eochair agus aon rud eile. ``null`` empties an ábhar, a bhfuil an t-aon bhealach a rá \"rud ar bith a thabhairt\": chumasc, Is mapáil folamh aon-uair agus bheadh a fhágáil go díreach na seirbhísí a bhí an bhabhta ag iarraidh a chaillfidh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A mapping of docker volume names and database names to ``postgres`` or ``mariadb``. Both volume spellings are emitted per application, because which one a host used depends on ``shared``, which is inventory-dependent and therefore unknowable from a checkout - and both spellings resolve to the same engine anyway."
msgstr "A mapáil ainmneacha toirt docker agus ainmneacha bunachar sonraí a ``postgres`` nó ``mariadb``. Tá an dá litriú toirte astaítear in aghaidh an iarratais, mar gheall ar a bhfuil ceann amháin a úsáidtear ag brath ar ``shared``, atá ag brath ar fhardal agus dá bhrí sin unknowable ó checkout - agus an dá litriú réiteach leis an inneall céanna ar aon nós."

# libretranslate
msgid "A marker value MUST be a non-empty string. If the marker key is present but the value is of the wrong YAML type, empty, or whitespace- only, the role's typing is broken: :func:`get_role_types` raises :class:`RoleTypeError` so the misconfiguration surfaces at the first call instead of silently degrading to a different type."
msgstr "A luach marcóir MUST a bheith ina teaghrán neamh-empty. Má tá an eochair marcóir i láthair ach tá an luach ar an gcineál YAML mícheart, folamh, nó bán- amháin, tá clóscríobh an ról briste: :func:`get_role_types` ardaitheoirí :class:`RoleTypeError` mar sin na dromchlaí misconfiguration ag an gcéad glaoch in ionad go ciúin táireach le cineál éagsúla."

# libretranslate
msgid "A matching `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` variable defined anywhere in Ansible variable scope (inventory, group vars, host vars)."
msgstr "A meaitseáil `SYSTEM_EMAIL_<KEY>` athróg sainithe in áit ar bith i raon feidhme athróg Ansible (fardal, vars grúpa, vars óstach)."

# libretranslate
msgid "A message prepared for an HTML-mode translation request."
msgstr "Teachtaireacht ullmhaithe le haghaidh iarratas aistriúcháin HTML-mode."

# libretranslate
msgid "A minted Tor v3 onion key and its ``HiddenServiceDir`` file contents."
msgstr "Tor v minted3 eochair oinniún agus a ``HiddenServiceDir`` ábhar comhaid."

# libretranslate
msgid "A missing event indicates a coverage regression in the deploy chain (typically: a once-flag swallowed an include before the role could run)."
msgstr "Léiríonn imeacht ar iarraidh athchéimniú clúdach sa slabhra imscaradh (de ghnáth: shlogtar bradach uair amháin sula bhféadfadh an ról a reáchtáil)."

# libretranslate
msgid "A missing secret resolves to an empty string in workflow expressions. The workflow run starts and proceeds normally until the token-minting step:"
msgstr "Réitíonn rún ar iarraidh le teaghrán folamh in abairtí sreabhadh oibre. Tosaíonn an sreabhadh oibre agus fáltais de ghnáth go dtí an chéim chomhartha-minting:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A module MAY read tool-specific environment overrides (e.g. `ACTIONLINT_VERSION`, `RUFF_PIP_SPEC`) at call time."
msgstr "A modúl MAY léamh overrides timpeallacht uirlis-sonrach (e.g. `ACTIONLINT_VERSION`, `RUFF_PIP_SPEC`) ag am glaoch."

# libretranslate
msgid "A module name MUST match the lowercase snake_case of the tool it installs:"
msgstr "A ainm modúl MUST mheaitseáil leis an níos ísle snake_case den uirlis a shuiteálann sé:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A monitored declared addon whose pinned ``version`` is behind the candidate's ``latest`` becomes a :class:`VersionSuggestion`."
msgstr "A monatóireacht a dhearbhú addon a pinned ``version`` Tá taobh thiar de na iarrthóir ``latest`` thiocfaidh chun bheith ina :class:`VersionSuggestion`."

# libretranslate
msgid "A name with more than one URL is a conflict the caller decides about; this function reports rather than resolves it."
msgstr "Tá ainm le níos mó ná URL amháin coimhlint chinneann an glaoiteoir faoi; tuarascálacha fheidhm seo seachas réitíonn sé."

# libretranslate
msgid "A new addon surfaced by a catalog adapter that is not yet declared."
msgstr "A addon nua dromchla ag adapter chatalóg nach bhfuil dearbhaithe go fóill."

# libretranslate
msgid "A new app MUST:"
msgstr "A app nua MUST:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A new database backend is added by extending `_ENGINES` — the rest of the module is engine-agnostic."
msgstr "Tá cúltaca bunachar nua seo a leanas trí leathnú `_ENGINES` — is é an chuid eile den mhodúl inneall-agnostic."

# libretranslate
msgid "A new helper MUST live in the subfolder that matches its responsibility. New responsibilities MAY motivate a new subfolder, but MUST NOT flatten back into the top level."
msgstr "A MUST cúntóir nua beo san fhofhillteán a oireann a fhreagracht. Freagrachtaí nua MAY spreagadh subfolder nua, ach NÍ MÓR leacaithe ar ais isteach sa leibhéal barr."

# libretranslate
msgid "A new key MUST be placed in `RESOLUTION_ORDER` after every key it depends on, and the administrator key table MUST be updated to document the new field."
msgstr "A MUST eochair nua a chur i `RESOLUTION_ORDER` tar éis gach eochair braitheann sé ar, agus an riarthóir MUST tábla eochair a thabhairt cothrom le dáta chun an réimse nua a dhoiciméadú."

# libretranslate
msgid "A new shared service MUST:"
msgstr "Seirbhís chomhroinnte nua MUST:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A no-variant `mode=reinstall` as the reaction to a failed variant or a code change. Only rows 1 and 4 omit `variant=`. To retry one failing variant, pin it with row 2; never restart the whole matrix to retry a single variant."
msgstr "Níl aon athrú `mode=reinstall` mar an imoibriú le malairt theip nó athrú cód. Níl ach sraitheanna 1 agus 4 Déan teagmháil `variant=`. Chun retry leagan amháin ag teip, bioráin sé le chéile 2; riamh atosú an maitrís ar fad a retry leagan amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A number is that many rows; anything else is a selection token (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`) and the start is the first regular row it names. Resuming at a role beats counting rows by hand: the ranking shifts whenever a variant is added, so the index that meant 'carry on behind nextcloud' yesterday means something else today, while the token still says it."
msgstr "Tá roinnt go sraitheanna go leor; Is rud ar bith eile a token rogha (:mod:`utils.github.variant.selection`) agus is é an tús an chéad tsraith rialta ainmneacha sé. Ag glacadh leis ag róil buillí comhaireamh sraitheanna de láimh: na shifts rangú aon uair a mhalairt leis, mar sin an t-innéacs a chiallaigh 'carradh ar chúl nextcloud' Ciallaíonn inné rud éigin eile lá atá inniu ann, cé go deir an chomhartha fós é."

# libretranslate
msgid "A parsed README: everything before the first H2, then its H2 blocks."
msgstr "A README parsed: gach rud roimh an chéad H2, ansin a H2 bloic."

# libretranslate
msgid "A path is yielded iff it survives both the in-process skip-dir pruning of :func:`iter_project_files` and the ``.gitignore`` match."
msgstr "Tá cosán thoradh iff mhaireann sé an bearradh scipe-dir in-próiseas :func:`iter_project_files` agus an ``.gitignore`` cluiche."

# libretranslate
msgid "A per-tool module MAY import from `utils.cache` (for `PROJECT_ROOT`) and from stdlib."
msgstr "iompórtáil MAY modúl per-tool ó `utils.cache` (le haghaidh `PROJECT_ROOT`) agus ó stdlib."

# libretranslate
msgid "A per-tool module MUST NOT import another per-tool module. Shared logic flows through `utils.install.primitives`, `utils.install.pip`, `utils.install.npm`, `utils.install.github_release`, and `utils.install.system_pkg` only."
msgstr "A modúl in aghaidh an-ol NACH allmhairiú eile in aghaidh an-ol modúl. Sreabhadh loighic roinnte trí `utils.install.primitives`, `utils.install.pip`, `utils.install.npm`, `utils.install.github_release`, agus `utils.install.system_pkg` ach amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A persona scenario MUST fail loudly when its contracted journey cannot execute end-to-end. A silent `test.skip(...)` on runtime detection of \"no logout button\", \"no authenticated surface\", or \"no admin UI marker\" is FORBIDDEN. Silent skips hide real regressions (broken OIDC mapping, removed logout button, misconfigured oauth2-proxy, drifted UI selectors) behind a green deploy."
msgstr "Teipeann ar chás persona go hard nuair nach féidir a thuras conradh a fhorghníomhú deireadh le deireadh. A adh `test.skip(...)` ar bhrath runtime \"aon cnaipe logáil isteach\", \"aon dromchla fíordheimhnithe\", nó \"aon marcóir Chomhéadain admin\" Is FORBIDDEN. Scipeanna Silent cheilt aischéimnithe fíor (mapáil OIDC briste, cnaipe logála amach a bhaint, oauth a mhaolú2-proxy, roghnóir Chomhéadain drifted) taobh thiar de glas imscaradh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A persona scenario that only logs in and logs out is NOT enough. After the auth chain settles (or directly on the role surface when no auth is required), every persona MUST drive a real, app-specific interaction so the spec proves the role is responsive to user input, not just reachable."
msgstr "Tá cás persona go logs ach amháin i agus logs amach NACH leor. Tar éis Socraíonn an slabhra auth (nó go díreach ar an dromchla ról nuair nach bhfuil aon auth ag teastáil), gach persona MUST tiomáint idirghníomhaíocht fíor, app-sonrach mar sin go gcruthóidh an spec an ról atá freagrach as ionchur úsáideora, ní reachable."

# libretranslate
msgid "A personal digital sovereignty stack for individuals controlling their own data."
msgstr "Stack ceannasachta digiteach pearsanta do dhaoine aonair a rialú a gcuid sonraí féin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A pin MUST be a quoted string, never an unquoted number. `\"\"` tracks the app default."
msgstr "A bioráin MUST a bheith ina teaghrán luaite, riamh uimhir unquoted. `\"\"` rianta an réamhshocraithe app."

# libretranslate
msgid "A pin the Docker updater (`image` + `version`) and the repository updater (`repository` + `ref`) do not reach names its upstream next to itself:"
msgstr "A bioráin an updater Docker (`image` + + + + `version`) agus an updater stór (`repository` + + + + `ref`) ná teacht ar ainmneacha a sruth in aice leis féin:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A pinned, isolated upstream sidecar."
msgstr "A pinned, scoite amach sruth."

# libretranslate
msgid "A pinned, source-audited upstream plugin."
msgstr "A pinned, foinse-fuaite breiseán upstream."

# libretranslate
msgid "A plug-and-go backup of the local backup tree to an external block device (typically a swappable USB drive). The transfer is hard-link deduplicated against the previous snapshot, so each plug-in yields a complete, browsable point-in-time copy without doubling disk usage."
msgstr "A cúltaca plug-agus-dul an crann cúltaca áitiúil le gléas bloc seachtrach (de ghnáth tiomáint USB swappable). Is é an t-aistriú crua-nasc deduplicated i gcoinne an pictiúr roimhe seo, mar sin gach breiseán-i táirgeacht iomlán, brabhsáil pointe-i-am cóip gan doubling úsáid diosca."

# libretranslate
msgid "A plugin MAY ship an appstore release that lags the pinned Nextcloud server major. In that case OCC emits the marker string `is not compatible with this version of the server` and exits non-zero. The pipeline MUST treat this as a non-fatal condition:"
msgstr "A breiseán MAY long scaoileadh appstore go lags an bhfreastalaí pinned Nextcloud mór. Sa chás sin astaíonn OCC an teaghrán marcóir `is not compatible with this version of the server` agus bealaí amach neamh-zero. An MUST píblíne a chóireáil seo mar riocht neamh-mharfach:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A plugin entry MAY set `mandatory: true`. This inverts the tolerance above: when the plugin is `enabled` for the current deployment but its install result is not `runnable` (incompatible with the pinned server major, or unavailable on the appstore), [01_install.yml](./01_install.yml) aborts the deployment with `ansible.builtin.fail` instead of emitting the skip warning."
msgstr "breiseán iontráil MAY leagtha `mandatory: true`. Inverts sé seo an caoinfhulaingt thuas: nuair a bhíonn an breiseán `enabled` don imscaradh reatha ach nach bhfuil a thoradh suiteála `runnable` (neamhoiriúnach leis an mór freastalaí pinned, nó ar fáil ar an appstore), [01Suiteáil.yml](./01_install.yml) aborts an imscaradh le `ansible.builtin.fail` in ionad a scaoileann an rabhadh skip."

# libretranslate
msgid "A pool of two or more stays a preference because the matrix already narrowed each row to one kind out of it: falling back to the other kind the run allowed is inside what the operator asked for, while failing the row is not. A run whose whole pool is unservable fails rather than leaving the pool."
msgstr "Fanann linn dhá nó níos mó rogha mar gheall ar an maitrís cúngú cheana féin gach as a chéile le cineál amháin as é: ag titim ar ais go dtí an cineál eile is é an rith a cheadaítear taobh istigh cad a d'iarr an t-oibreoir, agus ag teip nach bhfuil an tsraith. A reáchtáil a bhfuil a linn snámha ar fad theipeann unservable seachas ag fágáil an linn snámha."

# libretranslate
msgid "A post-application MCP reconciliation stage MUST run after all selected provider roles have provisioned and probed their endpoints. The stage MUST create one immutable discovery snapshot and reconcile Open WebUI, Flowise, Hermes, OpenClaw, and n8n from that snapshot. It MUST run after initial deployment, provider credential rotation, provider MCP enable/disable changes, and a standalone client container restart."
msgstr "A chéim athmhuintearas iar-iarratas MCP á reáchtáil tar éis gach ról soláthraí roghnaithe curtha ar fáil agus probed a n- endpointí. An chéim MUST chruthú Léim fionnachtana immutable amháin agus réiteach WebUI Oscailte, Flowise, Hermes, OpenClaw, agus n8n as an pictiúr. MUST sé ar siúl tar éis imscaradh tosaigh, uainíocht dintiúir soláthraí, soláthraí MCP chumasú / athruithe a dhíchumasú, agus atosú coimeádán cliant standalone."

# libretranslate
msgid "A practical long-term target is:"
msgstr "Is sprioc phraiticiúil fhadtéarmach:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A prefix cannot judge the container, so the probe keeps the verdict and the prefix only ever RAISES a timing -- the composed start period is the longest of the two, never the prefix's alone. Lowering it once would have cut a fifteen minute start window down to two."
msgstr "Ní féidir le réimír breitheamh an coimeádán, mar sin coimeádann an probe an fíorasc agus an réimír ach RAISES riamh uainiú - Is é an tréimhse tosaithe comhdhéanta an faide an dá, riamh an réimír ina n-aonar. Níos ísle go mbeadh sé a ghearradh uair amháin fuinneog tús nóiméad déag síos go dtí dhá."

# libretranslate
msgid "A prefix does something on the way past -- sending a smoke mail is the only one so far -- and deliberately cannot decide liveness. That separation is what lets a probe stay the single verdict."
msgstr "Déanann réimír rud éigin ar an mbealach seo caite - is é an t-aon phost deataigh a sheoladh an ceann amháin go dtí seo - agus d'aon ghnó ní féidir leis maireachtáil a chinneadh. Is é sin scaradh cad a ligeann probe fanacht ar an fíorasc amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A prefix mask leaves a contiguous run of low bits free, so per octet the addresses span exactly ``network_address`` to ``broadcast_address``. The cross product of those four ranges is the network, which makes the octet decomposition exact for any prefix length, aligned or not."
msgstr "Fágann masc réimír a reáchtáil leanúnach de giotán íseal saor in aisce, mar sin in aghaidh an octet na seoltaí réimse go díreach ``network_address`` go dtí ``broadcast_address``. Is é an táirge tras de na ceithre raonta an líonra, a dhéanann an dianscaoileadh octet cruinn d'aon fhad réimír, ailínithe nó nach bhfuil."

# libretranslate
msgid "A priority entry may pin axes (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), and the pin rides along into the retrigger: the entry never ran, so the run holds no evidence that the axes it named were the wrong ones. Only the name in front of the axis suffix is resolved against the statuses."
msgstr "Féadfaidh iontráil tosaíochta aiseanna bioráin (``web-app-zammad#1@compose+tor``), agus rides an bioráin chomh maith isteach sa retrigger: an iontráil riamh ar siúl, mar sin tá an reáchtáil aon fhianaise go raibh na haiseanna ainmnithe sé na cinn mícheart. Níl ach an t-ainm os comhair an iarmhír ais réitithe i gcoinne na stádas."

# libretranslate
msgid "A priority role can fall behind the discovery budget cut in every mode, so the run holds no job for it and :func:`failed_roles` cannot see it — it is neither green nor red, it simply never ran. Carrying it into the retrigger is the only way it ever gets deployed."
msgstr "Is féidir le ról tosaíochta titim taobh thiar de ghearradh buiséad fionnachtana i ngach modh, mar sin tá an rith aon phost chun é agus :func:`failed_roles` Ní féidir é a fheiceáil - níl sé glas ná dearg, ní raibh sé ar siúl go simplí. Is é a iompar isteach sa retrigger an t-aon bhealach a fhaigheann sé riamh imscaradh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A privacy-first foundation for enterprises running AI locally and keeping sensitive data on-prem."
msgstr "A bunús príobháideachta-an chéad d'fhiontair ag rith AI go háitiúil agus sonraí íogaire a choinneáil ar-réamh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A professional collaboration and identity management stack for modern organizations."
msgstr "Comhoibriú gairmiúil agus Stack bainistíochta aitheantais d'eagraíochtaí nua-aimseartha."

# libretranslate
msgid "A provider writes its credential to the token store during its own role run, and each client resolves the providers it may reach from that store. This role runs at the end of the server stage, after every provider has written and before the end-to-end tests read the converged state."
msgstr "Scríobhann soláthraí a chreidiúnacht chuig an siopa dearbhán le linn a ról féin a reáchtáil, agus réitíonn gach cliant na soláthraithe a d'fhéadfadh sé teacht ón siopa sin. Ritheann an ról ag deireadh an stáitse freastalaí, tar éis gach soláthraí scríofa agus roimh na tástálacha deireadh-le-deireadh léamh an stát converged."

# libretranslate
msgid "A proxy repo that holds a cached copy serves it when its remote is unreachable, regardless of `metadataMaxAge` (measured). `autoBlock` is therefore off: while a remote is auto-blocked Nexus answers `404 Remote Auto Blocked` instead of falling back to that cached copy. The mirror repos below only come into play when nothing is cached either."
msgstr "Freastalaíonn repo seachvótálaí a bhfuil cóip taisceadh air nuair a bhíonn a iargúlta unreachable, beag beann ar `metadataMaxAge` (tomhaiste). `autoBlock` dá bhrí sin, as: cé go bhfuil iargúlta uathoibríoch-blocked freagraí Nexus `404 Remote Auto Blocked` in ionad titim ar ais go dtí an chóip taisce. An repos scáthán thíos ach teacht i spraoi nuair nach bhfuil aon rud i dtaisce ceachtar."

# libretranslate
msgid "A question MUST NOT modify files, code, or state. Only explicit commands MAY."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR ceist a mhodhnú comhaid, cód, nó stát. Ach orduithe sainráite MAY."

# libretranslate
msgid "A rapid deployment stack for startups building software products and services."
msgstr "Stack imscaradh tapa do startups thógáil táirgí bogearraí agus seirbhísí."

# libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST NOT be written for a choice that a reader can recover from the code alone, such as a helper's signature or a local refactoring."
msgstr "NÍ MÓR taifead a scríobh le haghaidh rogha gur féidir le léitheoir a ghnóthú ón gcód ina n-aonar, mar shampla síniú cúntóir nó refactoring áitiúil."

# libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST be numbered in the order it was accepted, and its number MUST NOT be reused."
msgstr "A MUST taifead a uimhriú san ord glacadh leis, agus a uimhir NACH MÓR a athúsáid."

# libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST cover a decision whose reversal would be expensive: a contract between components, a data or naming shape other code depends on, or a rule that governs a whole subsystem."
msgstr "A MUST taifead chlúdach cinneadh a bheadh a aisiompú a bheith costasach: conradh idir comhpháirteanna, sonraí nó cruth ainmniú cód eile ag brath ar, nó riail a rialaíonn fochóras ar fad."

# libretranslate
msgid "A record MUST describe the decision as it stands today, including the alternatives that were weighed and why they lost, so a later reader can tell a deliberate constraint from an accident."
msgstr "MUST taifead cur síos ar an gcinneadh mar a sheasann sé inniu, lena n-áirítear na roghanna a bhí mheá agus cén fáth a chaill siad, mar sin is féidir le léitheoir níos déanaí a insint srian d'aon ghnó ó timpiste."

# libretranslate
msgid "A recover mirrors a snapshot into a live target directory (``rsync -a --delete``), so the target's current state would be lost without a net. The flow therefore first runs the role's deployed backup service (``systemctl start`` on the role's unit), which applies the usual differential backup logic to the live data before anything is overwritten. Roles subclass :class:`DirectoryRecovery`, set ``unit_pattern`` and ship a thin ``files/python/recover.py`` CLI around it (enforced by ``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_bkp_roles_have_recover.py``)."
msgstr "A ghnóthú scátháin a snapshot isteach eolaire sprioc beo (``rsync -a --delete``), mar sin bheadh an sprioc stáit reatha a bheith caillte gan glan. Ritheann an sreabhadh dá bhrí sin ar dtús an ról seirbhíse cúltaca imscaradh (``systemctl start`` ar aonad an róil), a bhfuil feidhm ag an loighic cúltaca difreálach is gnách leis na sonraí beo sula bhfuil aon rud overwritten. Róil fo-aicme :class:`DirectoryRecovery`, leagtha ``unit_pattern`` agus long tanaí ``files/python/recover.py`` CLI timpeall air (i bhfeidhm ag ``tests/lint/ansible/roles/test_bkp_roles_have_recover.py``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "A recurring property of these extensions is that many of them exist **only to bridge into another role**: `ldapauth` and `user_ldap` bridge to `svc-db-openldap`; `sociallogin`, `oidc-authenticator`, `OpenIDConnect`, `plg_system_keycloak`, and the WordPress OIDC plugin bridge to the SSO provider (`web-app-keycloak`); `wp-discourse` bridges to `web-app-discourse`; XWiki's `matomo` plugin bridges to `web-app-matomo`. Today that bridge is implicit. This requirement makes it explicit: **an addon that bridges to another role MUST declare the bridged service, and that service MUST be present in the role's `meta/services.yml`.**"
msgstr "Is maoin athfhillteach de na síntí go bhfuil go leor acu ann **ach amháin chun droichead isteach i ról eile**: `ldapauth` agus `user_ldap` droichead go dtí `svc-db-openldap`; `sociallogin`, `oidc-authenticator`, `OpenIDConnect`, `plg_system_keycloak`, agus an WordPress OIDC droichead breiseán chuig an soláthraí SSO (`web-app-keycloak`); `wp-discourse` droichid chuig `web-app-discourse`; XWiki ar `matomo` droichid breiseán chuig `web-app-matomo`. Sa lá atá inniu go bhfuil droichead intuigthe. Fágann an ceanglas seo go follasach: **a addon go droichid le ról eile MST dhearbhú an tseirbhís droichead, agus an tseirbhís sin MUST a bheith i láthair sa ról `meta/services.yml`.**"

# libretranslate
msgid "A red deploy skips the replay: the step carries no `always()`, so the runner state a failed deploy leaves behind never reaches the guide."
msgstr "A scipeanna imscaradh dearg an replay: déanann an chéim aon `always()`, mar sin ní shroicheann an dara háit duilleoga taobh thiar den treoir."

# libretranslate
msgid "A red job could not be reproduced by re-running its sweep, which is the property the whole rotation exists to provide."
msgstr "Ní fhéadfaí post dearg a atáirgeadh trí ath-reáchtáil a scuab, a bhfuil an mhaoin ann an uainíocht ar fad a chur ar fáil."

msgid "A regex over dotted octets, e.g. ``192\\.168\\.24\\.\\d+`` for a /24 or ``192\\.168\\.(24|25)\\.\\d+`` for a /23."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "A relative `include_tasks` resolves against the including file's directory when that file was reached by path, and against `tasks/` when it was reached through `tasks_from`. A file under `tasks/utils/` therefore loads from its own role and fails from the reconciler, unchanged. Every include below a `tasks_from` entrypoint MUST name a path that holds under both bases."
msgstr "gaol `include_tasks` réitíonn i gcoinne an comhad lena n-áirítear eolaire nuair a bhí an comhad sin bainte amach ag cosán, agus i gcoinne `tasks/` nuair a bhí sé bainte amach trí `tasks_from`. A comhad faoi `tasks/utils/` dá bhrí sin ualaí as a ról féin agus go mainneoidh as an réiteach, gan athrú. Gach san áireamh thíos `tasks_from` MUST iontráil ainm cosán atá i seilbh faoin dá boinn."

# libretranslate
msgid "A release tag (``vX.Y.Z``) is built the first time someone opens it. The browser shows a progress bar and reloads once the build is done. Tags never change, so each tag is built only once."
msgstr "Clib scaoilte (``vX.Y.Z``) tógtha an chéad uair a osclaíonn duine éigin é. Taispeánann an brabhsálaí barra dul chun cinn agus athluchtú nuair a dhéantar an tógáil. Clibeanna riamh athrú, mar sin tá gach chlib tógtha ach uair amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A release tag (`vX.Y.Z`) is built the first time someone opens it. The browser shows a progress bar and reloads once the build is done. Tags never change, so each tag is built only once."
msgstr "Clib scaoilte (`vX.Y.Z`) tógtha an chéad uair a osclaíonn duine éigin é. Taispeánann an brabhsálaí barra dul chun cinn agus athluchtú nuair a dhéantar an tógáil. Clibeanna riamh athrú, mar sin tá gach chlib tógtha ach uair amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A remote source (``[user@]host:/path``) is returned as-is with the default target (its colon is the rsync host separator). Otherwise a colon suffix is a restore target only when absolute; a relative suffix is rejected here (device parses those itself)."
msgstr "Foinse iargúlta (``[user@]host:/path``) ar ais mar-is leis an sprioc réamhshocraithe (Is é a colon an deighilteoir óstach rsync). Seachas sin tá iarmhír colon sprioc ar ais ach amháin nuair absalóideach; Tá iarmhír coibhneasta diúltaíodh anseo (parses gléas iad féin)."

# libretranslate
msgid "A rendered ``socialhome.toml`` is mounted alongside the environment file. It carries exactly one setting — ``[standalone].external_url`` — because that value has no ``SH_*`` environment equivalent upstream and federation pairing returns ``422 NOT_CONFIGURED`` without it."
msgstr "A rinneadh ``socialhome.toml`` Tá suite taobh leis an comhad comhshaoil. Déanann sé go díreach suíomh amháin - ``[standalone].external_url`` - toisc nach bhfuil aon luach ``SH_*`` comhshaoil cothrom le sruth agus beatha tuairisceáin pairing ``422 NOT_CONFIGURED`` gan é."

