# libretranslate
msgid "A single commit (or a tight related sequence) lands the whole role addition."
msgstr "tiomantas aonair (nó ord daingean a bhaineann) tailte an Chomh maith leis an ról iomlán."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single commit (or a tight, related sequence) lands the whole role addition; no half-scaffolded intermediate commits."
msgstr "tiomantas aonair (nó daingean, ord a bhaineann) tailte an Chomh maith leis an ról iomlán; aon ciorruithe idirmheánach leath-scaffolded."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single entry a catalog adapter surfaced for relevance + version review."
msgstr "A iontráil amháin adapter chatalóg dromchla le haghaidh ábharthacht + leagan athbhreithniú."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single grammar covers every per-line, per-block, and per-file opt-out across the test suite. See ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` for the catalog of valid rule keys, their placement, and the test that consumes each."
msgstr "Clúdaíonn gramadach amháin gach in aghaidh an-líne, per-block, agus rogha-amach per-file ar fud an tsraith tástála. Féach ar ``docs/contributing/actions/testing/suppression.md`` do chatalóg na heochracha riail bailí, a socrúcháin, agus an tástáil a itheann gach."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single paragraph (one or two sentences) immediately below the H1. It MUST explain what kind of commands live in the directory. It MUST NOT name the sub-commands explicitly. It MUST stand on its own when extracted by the CLI help system, which collapses multi-line paragraphs into a single line."
msgstr "Mír amháin (pianbhreith amháin nó dhá phianbhreith) láithreach faoi bhun an H1. MUST sé a mhíniú cén cineál orduithe beo ar an eolaire. NÍ MÓR é ainm na fo-orduithe go sainráite. MUST seasamh ar a chuid féin nuair a bhaintear ag an gcóras cabhrach CLI, a thiteann míreanna il-líne isteach i líne amháin."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single volume"
msgstr "A toirt amháin"

# libretranslate
msgid "A single wildcard replaces 15+ per-shape entries (`* make *`, `docker *`, `gh api *`, `grep *`, `head *`, `tail *`, `tee *`, `wc *`, `echo *`, `pkill *`, `* > /tmp/*`, `*=* python* *`, `gh issue *`, `gh run *`, `make *`) that existed purely as workarounds for the sandbox auto-allow heuristic declining on env-prefixes, redirects, pipes, and quoted args. With `Bash(*)` the allowlist no longer rots as new command shapes emerge; the gating responsibility moves entirely to `ask` (mutating verbs) and `deny` (structurally unsafe shapes)."
msgstr "Tagann cárta fiáin amháin 15+ iontrálacha in aghaidh an-cruth (`* make *`, `docker *`, `gh api *`, `grep *`, `head *`, `tail *`, `tee *`, `wc *`, `echo *`, `pkill *`, `* > /tmp/*`, `*=* python* *`, `gh issue *`, `gh run *`, `make *`) a bhí ann ach amháin mar workarounds don bosca gainimh auto-cheadú líneáil heuristic ar env-prefixes, atreoruithe, píopaí, agus Args luaite. Le haghaidh `Bash(*)` an liosta a thuilleadh rots mar cruthanna orduithe nua chun cinn; bogann an fhreagracht gating go hiomlán chun `ask` (briathra mutating) agus `deny` (cruthanna struchtúrtha neamhshábháilte)."

# libretranslate
msgid "A single-element list holding the expanded spec list, so the caller receives the list itself rather than its first element."
