# libretranslate
msgid "A stack role (ships a compose template) is offered ``compose`` and ``swarm``; a host-only role is offered ``host``. The two are mutually exclusive: swarm needs a stack, host configures the machine instead."
msgstr "Ról chairn (longa teimpléad a chumadh) Tá sé ar fáil ``compose`` agus ``swarm``; Tá ról óstach ar fáil ``host``. Tá an dá eisiach go frithpháirteach: riachtanais Swarm Stack, configures óstach an meaisín ina ionad."

# libretranslate
msgid "A static-analysis pass (added in [tests/lint/ansible/roles/web-app/playwright/test_env_keys_used.py](../../tests/lint/ansible/roles/web-app/playwright/test_env_keys_used.py)) surfaced multiple roles that **declared** the `BIBER_*` env keys but never read them in the spec; the env file was prepared, the spec was never written. The most prominent example is `web-app-joomla`: it ships an OIDC variant (`plg_system_keycloak`) and an LDAP variant (core LDAP auth plugin) per [006 - Service-gated Playwright tests](README.md#archive), but the Playwright spec only exercises the admin login. A non-admin biber landing-page assertion is missing and would catch RBAC group-mapping drift introduced by 004."
msgstr "A pas statach-anailís (Chuir in [tests/lint/ansible/roles/web-app/playwright/test_env_keys_used.py](../../tests/lint/ansible/roles/web-app/playwright/test_env_keys_used.py)) róil éagsúla dromchla go **dearbhaithe** an `BIBER_*` env eochracha ach riamh iad a léamh sa spec; ullmhaíodh an comhad env, ní raibh an spec scríofa. Is é an sampla is suntasaí `web-app-joomla`: long sé leagan OIDC (`plg_system_keycloak`) agus leagan LDAP (croí LDAP breiseán auth) in aghaidh an [006 - Seirbhís-gated tástálacha Playwright](README.md#archive), ach an spec Playwright cleachtaí ach an logáil isteach admin. Tá dearbhú neamh-admin biber tuirlingthe-leathanach ar iarraidh agus bheadh a ghabháil sruth grúpa RBAC isteach ag 004."

# libretranslate
msgid "A subclass of str to represent vault-encrypted strings."
msgstr "A fo-aicme de str chun ionadaíocht a dhéanamh cordaí cruinneachán- Criptithe."

# libretranslate
msgid "A suite is turned off only when every job of it came back green; one that failed, was cancelled or never ran at all keeps it on the retrigger, so a retrigger spends its runners on what is not yet proven."
msgstr "Tá sraith iompaithe amach ach amháin nuair a tháinig gach post de sé ar ais glas; ceann amháin gur theip, Cuireadh ar ceal nó riamh ar siúl ar chor ar bith Coinníonn sé ar an retrigger, mar sin caitheann retrigger a dara háit ar cad nach bhfuil cruthaithe go fóill."

# libretranslate
msgid "A superseded record MUST stay in place with its status changed and a link to the record that replaces it, because the reasoning it carries is what makes the replacement legible."
msgstr "A taifead in áit MUST fanacht i bhfeidhm lena stádas athrú agus nasc leis an taifead a ionad, mar gheall ar an réasúnaíocht a dhéanann sé cad a dhéanann an inléite athsholáthair."

# libretranslate
msgid "A supported native MCP endpoint with an enforceable tool policy."
msgstr "A endpoint dúchais MCP tacaíocht le polasaí uirlis infhorfheidhmithe."

# libretranslate
msgid "A suppression marker is a comment carrying one or more rule keys:"
msgstr "Tá marcóir faoi chois trácht a iompar eochracha riail amháin nó níos mó:"

# libretranslate
msgid "A surface is reachable only while a peer that uses it is deployed, so both keys resolve to the ``in group_names`` form the rest of the tree uses, and to ``False`` when a role has no peer at all. An explicitly configured ``enabled``/``shared`` always wins, so config stays the override channel. Keying on peer PRESENCE rather than on a peer's own value is required: a re-entrant read under ``_RENDER_GUARD`` returns the unrendered dict."
msgstr "Ní féidir dromchla a bhaint amach ach amháin nuair a úsáideann piaraí é a imscaradh, mar sin réitíonn an dá eochracha leis an ``in group_names`` foirm an chuid eile de na húsáidí crann, agus chun ``False`` nuair nach bhfuil ról ar bith piaraí ar chor ar bith. Cumraigh go sainráite ``enabled``/ Baile``shared`` bua i gcónaí, mar sin fanacht config an cainéal override. Tá gá le hathrú ar PRESENCE piaraí seachas ar luach piaraí féin: léamh aitheanta faoi ``_RENDER_GUARD`` tuairisceáin an deachtóir gan aithne."

# libretranslate
msgid "A swarm task is attached to several site-local networks at once, so a service that must bind to one specific network cannot be told \"pick a site-local address\" - it needs a matcher for the one subnet it owns."
msgstr "Tá tasc swarm ceangailte le roinnt líonraí suíomh-áitiúil ag an am céanna, mar sin ní féidir seirbhís nach mór ceangal le líonra ar leith amháin a insint \"Pioc seoladh áitiúil láithreán\" - ní mór é a mheaitseáil don subnet amháin úinéireacht sé."

# libretranslate
msgid "A sweep over all 85 application roles for provider references (`openai`, `ollama`, `llm`, `anthropic`, `aiprovider`) in `meta/`, `vars/` and `templates/` returns only `dashboard`, `flowise`, `hermes`, `litellm`, `matrix`, `minio`, `nextcloud`, `openclaw` and `openwebui`. Everything below the AI-native roles is therefore unwired today."
msgstr "A sweep thar gach 85 róil iarratais le haghaidh tagairtí soláthraí (`openai`, `ollama`, `llm`, `anthropic`, `aiprovider`) i `meta/`, `vars/` agus `templates/` tuairisceáin ach amháin `dashboard`, `flowise`, `hermes`, `litellm`, `matrix`, `minio`, `nextcloud`, `openclaw` agus `openwebui`. Tá gach rud faoi bhun na róil AI-native dá bhrí sin unwired inniu."

# libretranslate
msgid "A target other than localhost is a remote ``[user@]host`` reached over ssh."
msgstr "Tá sprioc eile seachas localhost iargúlta ``[user@]host`` shroich thar ssh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A task whose `when:` evaluates compose-only at deploy time (e.g. `when: DEPLOYMENT_MODE != 'swarm'` or `when: DEPLOYMENT_MODE == 'compose'`) never reaches a swarm host, so `compose <verb>` / `chdir: directories.instance` inside that task body is legitimate. This module gives the lints a heuristic to recognise that gate without parsing YAML."
msgstr "tasc a bhfuil a `when:` meastóireacht a dhéanamh ar chumadh-amháin ag am a imscaradh (e.g. `when: DEPLOYMENT_MODE != 'swarm'` nó `when: DEPLOYMENT_MODE == 'compose'`) riamh sroicheann óstach swarm, mar sin `compose <verb>` / Baile `chdir: directories.instance` taobh istigh go bhfuil comhlacht tasc dlisteanach. Tugann an modúl seo na lints a heuristic a aithint go geata gan parsáil YAML."

# libretranslate
msgid "A templated value (`\"{{ ... }}\"`), whether a `lookup(..., 'secrets.credentials.<name>')` call or another variable reference, is accepted; a bare scalar literal (string without `{{`, or a raw int/bool) is a hard-coded secret and is rejected."
msgstr "Luach teimpléid (`\"{{ ... }}\"`), cibé acu an `lookup(..., 'secrets.credentials.<name>')` glaoch nó tagairt athróg eile, Glactar leis; scalar lom litriúil (teaghrán gan sreang `{{`, nó amh int / bonn) Is rúnda crua-chódaithe agus diúltaíodh é."

# libretranslate
msgid "A term unknown to the play-local registry (no app in the play declares it) falls back to the role-wide static registry read from roles_dir, the same source the sys-service-loader iterates. Such a key resolves with its provider role and all deployment flags computed against the play (typically all false). Only a term unknown to BOTH registries raises."
msgstr "téarma anaithnid ar an gclárlann áitiúil spraoi (aon app sa spraoi Dearbhaíonn sé) titim ar ais go dtí an clárlann statach ró-leathan léamh ó roles_dir, an fhoinse chéanna na iterates steals-seirbhíse-luchtaitheoir. Réitíonn a leithéid de eochair lena ról soláthraí agus gach bratach imscaradh ríomh i gcoinne an dráma (de ghnáth go léir bréagach). Ní ardaíonn ach téarma nach eol do chlárlanna BOTH."

# libretranslate
msgid "A tightened protection rule turns silently corrupted translations - a rewritten path, a dissolved markdown target - into entries this reports, so the next translation run redoes them. The markup comparison catches what masking cannot: a bracket the translator added or dropped next to a protected span leaves every span intact and still breaks the link."
msgstr "Casadh riail cosanta tightened aistriúcháin truaillithe go ciúin - cosán athscríofa, sprioc markdown díscaoilte - iontrálacha na tuarascálacha seo, mar sin an chéad aistriúchán eile a reáchtáil redoes iad. Gabhálacha comparáide marcála cad nach féidir le mascing: lúibín chuir an t-aistritheoir nó thit in aice le réimse cosanta duilleoga gach réimse slán agus fós bhriseann an nasc."

# libretranslate
msgid "A tiny boolean filter language over :class:`ComplexityRow` fields."
msgstr "teanga scagaire beag bídeach níos mó ná :class:`ComplexityRow` réimsí."

# libretranslate
msgid "A token naming a role the discovery query does not return at all is reported too, but as a warning, whether or not it pins axes: the diff-derived whitelist legitimately names roles the envelope filters out, and it pins the variants a change reaches. Role names themselves are checked against `roles/` before the run starts (scripts/github/resolve/effective_whitelist.sh), so a typo is caught there rather than swallowed here."
msgstr "A chomhartha a ainmniú ról nach bhfuil an cheist fionnachtana ar ais ar chor ar bith a thuairisciú freisin, ach mar rabhadh, cibé acu nó nach bhfuil sé pins axes: an diff-derived whitelist rólanna go dlisteanach na scagairí clúdach amach, agus bioráin sé na leaganacha sroicheann athrú. Ról ainmneacha iad féin a sheiceáil i gcoinne `roles/` sula dtosaíonn an rith (scripts/github/resolve/effective_whitelist.sh), mar sin tá typo gafa ann seachas shlogtar anseo."

# libretranslate
msgid "A token that narrows nothing beyond the role name is answered by existence: it asks for the role in whatever axes the rotation picks, so any discovered row satisfies it. Rows are keyed by ``(name, variant)`` and a variant is an int, so looking such a token up variant-first can only miss, which reported every collapsed priority entry as matching nothing and left a role that really had no row indistinguishable from one with a full set."
msgstr "A chomhartha go gcúngaíonn rud ar bith níos faide ná an t-ainm ról atá fhreagair ann: iarrann sé ar an ról i cibé aiseanna an picks uainíochta, mar sin aon rá amach sásaíonn sé. Tá Rows eochair ag ``(name, variant)`` agus tá leagan orlach, mar sin ag lorg a leithéid de chomhartha suas athraitheach-is féidir a chailleann ach amháin, a thuairiscigh gach iontráil tosaíochta tubaiste mar meaitseáil rud ar bith agus d'fhág ról go raibh i ndáiríre aon as a chéile indistinguishably ó amháin le sraith iomlán."

# libretranslate
msgid "A token with no directory under ``roles/`` encodes to itself: it is a sentinel like ``__ALL__``, or a role the tree does not hold, and neither has a heading or a category to read."
msgstr "chomhartha gan aon eolaire faoi ``roles/`` ionchódú dó féin: tá sé ina sentinel cosúil ``__ALL__``, nó ról nach bhfuil an crann i seilbh, agus nach bhfuil ceannteideal nó catagóir a léamh."

# libretranslate
msgid "A tools-only server never has to stream, so every response is a plain JSON body and no SSE session state exists to get wrong."
msgstr "A fhreastalaí uirlisí-amháin riamh go bhfuil a sruth, mar sin tá gach freagra comhlacht JSON plain agus níl aon stát seisiún SSE a fháil mícheart."

