# libretranslate
msgid "Allows JavaScript to substitute a value for an unset environment variable. Reserved for a value the code itself owns and no role renders. Normalising to `\"\"`, `\"[]\"`, `false`, `0` or another `process.env` entry needs no marker."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn JavaScript luach a chur in ionad athróg timpeallacht gan leagan. Cúlchiste le haghaidh luach úinéireacht an cód féin agus ní dhéanann aon ról. Ag gnáthú `\"\"`, `\"[]\"`, `false`, `0` nó eile `process.env` riachtanais iontrála aon marcóir."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows `*_CONTAINER_ADDRESS | quote` in a role task file. Reserved for sites that never see the swarm `$(...)` fragment (`DEPLOYMENT_MODE == 'compose'`-gated tasks, `compose_mode_force` roles) or consumers that re-evaluate the argument themselves."
msgstr "Seirbhís do Chustaiméirí `*_CONTAINER_ADDRESS | quote` i gcomhad tasc ról. Cúltaca do láithreáin nach bhfeiceann an Swarm `$(...)` il il (`DEPLOYMENT_MODE == 'compose'`- tascanna gated, `compose_mode_force` Róil) nó tomhaltóirí a ath-evaluate an argóint féin."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows `... | bool == True/False/true/false` when a real tri-state guard is intended (distinguishing `None` from `False`)."
msgstr "Seirbhís do Chustaiméirí `... | bool == True/False/true/false` nuair a bhíonn garda fíor-thrialach beartaithe (idirdhealú `None` ó `False`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a Jinja expression to stand as a mapping key under `roles/*/meta/`. Ansible renders the values of an `include_vars` payload and leaves the keys as written, so the consumer receives the source text. Marker goes on or directly above the line."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn léiriú Jinja chun seasamh mar eochair mapála faoi `roles/*/meta/`. Déanann Ansible na luachanna de `include_vars` pálasta agus fágann na heochracha mar atá scríofa, mar sin faigheann an tomhaltóir an téacs foinse. Téann Marker ar an líne nó go díreach os cionn na líne."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `*.sh.j2` to exist. Default path: ship the script as a plain `.sh` under `files/shell/` and pass its values as `ExecStart` arguments or `Environment=` entries, because shellcheck, the repository's `.sh` guards and every test skip a Jinja template, so nothing reads what actually runs on the host. Reserved for a script whose shape is generated, not just its values. Place the marker BELOW the shebang, never above it, and prefer the Jinja comment form so it does not reach the rendered script."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `*.sh.j2` a bheith ann. cosán réamhshocraithe: long an script mar plain `.sh` faoi bhun `files/shell/` agus pas a luachanna mar `ExecStart` argóintí nó `Environment=` iontrálacha, mar shampla, an stór ar `.sh` gardaí agus gach tástáil skip teimpléad Jinja, mar sin léann rud ar bith cad a ritheann i ndáiríre ar an óstach. Cúlchiste le haghaidh script a bhfuil cruth a ghintear, ní hamháin a luachanna. Cuir an marcóir BELOW an shebang, riamh os a chionn, agus is fearr leis an bhfoirm comment Jinja mar sin ní dhéanann sé teacht ar an script a rinneadh."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `.j2` template to write the software's name, domain or URL as a literal. Default path: render `SOFTWARE_NAME`, `SOFTWARE_DOMAIN`, `SOFTWARE_URL` or `ORGANIZATION`, which `group_vars/all/00_general.yml` declares once and derives from each other, so a rename reaches the template too. Reserved for a literal that must survive a rename, such as an identifier a third party issued under the old name."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `.j2` teimpléad a scríobh ainm na bogearraí, fearainn nó URL mar litriúil. cosán réamhshocraithe: rindreáil `SOFTWARE_NAME`, `SOFTWARE_DOMAIN`, `SOFTWARE_URL` nó `ORGANIZATION`, a, `group_vars/all/00_general.yml` Dearbhaíonn uair amháin agus a dhíorthaíonn óna chéile, mar sin sroicheann athainmniú an teimpléad freisin. Cúlchiste le haghaidh litriúil nach mór maireachtáil athainmniú, mar shampla aitheantóir tríú páirtí a eisíodh faoin seanainm."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `.py` file to carry a literal role-file path instead of the matching `ROLE_FILE_*` constant from `utils.roles.mapping`. Reserved for tests asserting the constant's value, migration scripts, or doc strings."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `.py` comhad a dhéanamh ról-comhaid litriúil in ionad an meaitseáil `ROLE_FILE_*` tairiseach ó `utils.roles.mapping`. Cúlchiste le haghaidh tástálacha a dhearbhú an tairiseach luach, scripteanna imirce, nó teaghráin doc."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `container exec` / `container inspect` target that does not route through the `container_address` lookup. Reserved for a container ID already resolved at `delegate_to` runtime (`*_LOCAL_CID`), where the lookup would return a manager-only subshell, and for deliberate bare-name partner probes gated on compose co-location."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `container exec` / Baile `container inspect` sprioc nach bhfuil bealach tríd an `container_address` cuma. Cúlchiste le haghaidh ID coimeádán réiteach cheana féin ag `delegate_to` runtime (`*_LOCAL_CID`), i gcás ina mbeadh an Lookup ar ais bainisteoir-amháin subshell, agus d'aon ghnó probes páirtí lom-ainm gated ar chumadh comh-suíomh."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `container_address`-derived target to be reached from a `command: argv:` list, which runs no shell to evaluate the swarm `$(...)` fragment. Reserved for roles pinned to compose via `compose_mode_force`, where the lookup can only ever yield a bare name."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `container_address`-sprioc a bhaint amach ó `command: argv:` liosta, a ritheann aon bhlaosc a mheas an Swarm `$(...)` il. Cúlchiste le haghaidh róil pinned a chumadh trí `compose_mode_force`, nuair is féidir leis an Lookup a thabhairt ach riamh ainm lom."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `loop_var` to take the name of a variable declared in `group_vars/**` or in a role's `vars`/`defaults`. Inside the loop that name carries the item, so every lookup, template and nested include reading it sees the item instead, and ansible only warns. Reserved for a loop whose body reads the name as the item on purpose, typically because the item IS that value: state which meaning the body relies on."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `loop_var` a chur ar an ainm athróg dearbhaithe i `group_vars/**` nó i ról `vars`/ Baile`defaults`. Taobh istigh den lúb a dhéanann ainm an mhír, mar sin gach Lookup, teimpléad agus neadaithe san áireamh léamh Feiceann sé an mhír ina ionad sin, agus ansible rabhadh ach amháin. Cúlchiste le haghaidh lúb a léann a chorp an t-ainm mar an mhír ar na críche, de ghnáth mar gheall ar IS an mhír an luach: stát a chiallaíonn an comhlacht ag brath ar."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` `min_storage` to exceed the measured compressed size of its own `image:`/`version:` by more than 1 GB. MUST be paired with a `Reason:` on the same comment line naming what occupies the space. Reserved for services whose data volume genuinely dominates the footprint; the default path is to lower the value, because an over-declared budget makes a host look too small and prunes a cache the deploy did not need to lose."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` `min_storage` níos mó ná an méid comhbhrúite tomhaiste dá chuid féin `image:`/ Baile`version:` ag níos mó ná 1 GB. MUST a péireáilte le `Reason:` ar an líne tráchta chéanna ainmniú cad a áitíonn an spás. Cúlchiste le haghaidh seirbhísí a bhfuil a méid sonraí tionchar iarbhír an lorg; Is é an cosán réamhshocraithe a ísliú an luach, mar gheall ar a dhéanann buiséad ró-declared lorg óstach ró-bheag agus prunes taisce nach raibh an imscaradh gá a chailleadh."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` entry whose image ships no `HEALTHCHECK` to declare none either. Default path: add `healthcheck:` to the entry, because a container without a probe counts as healthy the moment its process starts — which is how a service that came back empty passes a restore drill. Reserved for containers nothing can probe: a one-shot process that exits, or an image with neither a port nor a shell."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `roles/*/meta/services.yml` iontráil a bhfuil longa íomhá aon `HEALTHCHECK` a dhearbhú ceachtar. cosán réamhshocraithe: cuir `healthcheck:` leis an iontráil, toisc go chomhaireamh coimeádán gan probe chomh sláintiúil an nóiméad a thosaíonn a phróiseas - a bhfuil conas a théann seirbhís a tháinig ar ais folamh druil ar ais. Cúlchiste le haghaidh coimeádáin is féidir aon rud probe: próiseas aon-lámhaigh a exits, nó íomhá le ní port ná bhlaosc."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` `services.<key>` entry to reference a service key that is NOT declared as a top-level entry in `meta/services.yml`. Reserved for resolver-only matrix hooks (typically on invokable infrastructure roles) whose variant entries pin the round's companion topology via service-key flags the resolver maps to provider roles, with no real consumer contract in the base meta."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` `services.<key>` iontráil tagairt eochair seirbhíse NACH bhfuil dearbhaithe mar iontráil barrleibhéil i `meta/services.yml`. Cúlchiste le haghaidh crúcaí maitrís réiteora-amháin (de ghnáth ar róil bhonneagair invokable) a n-iontrálacha leagan bioráin topology chompánach an bhabhta trí sheirbhís-eochair bratacha na léarscáileanna réiteora le róil soláthraí, gan aon chonradh tomhaltóirí fíor sa meta bonn."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` leaf override of an attribute whose base value in `meta/services.yml` is a static literal. Place on the override line in `variants.yml`. Use only when the consumer chain is provably immune to the variant-merge propagation gap; the default is to make the base value dynamic via `\"{{ '<role>' in group_names }}\"`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `roles/*/meta/variants.yml` override duille tréith a bhfuil a luach bonn i `meta/services.yml` Is litriúil statach. Áit ar an líne override i `variants.yml`. Bain úsáid as ach amháin nuair a bhíonn an slabhra tomhaltóirí díolmhaithe go provably chun an bhearna iomadú malairtithe a chumasadh; is é an réamhshocraithe a dhéanamh ar an luach bonn dinimiciúil trí `\"{{ '<role>' in group_names }}\"`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a `services.<key>.healthcheck` that no `lookup('container_healthcheck', …)` call renders. Default path: add the lookup to the service block, because an unrendered declaration reads like the service is watched while the compose file carries no probe. Reserved for a call the static resolver cannot attribute — mastodon renders every service through a macro whose `service_name` is a macro parameter."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn a `services.<key>.healthcheck` Nach bhfuil aon `lookup('container_healthcheck', …)` rindreáil glaoch. Default cosán: cuir an cuma leis an mbloc seirbhíse, mar gheall ar léann dearbhú neamhréadaithe cosúil leis an tseirbhís faire agus déanann an comhad a chumadh aon probe. Cúlchiste le haghaidh glao nach féidir leis an réiteoir statach tréith - crannodon rindreáil gach seirbhís trí macra a `service_name` Is paraiméadar macra."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a bare curl invocation without the `curl` filter or inline `--max-time`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn invocation lom curl gan an `curl` scagaire nó inlíne `--max-time`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a conditional `resolve_host_cid` include whose `<PREFIX>_HOST_NODE` a `delegate_to` in the same role reads. Marker goes on or directly above the include's `- name:`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn coinníollach `resolve_host_cid` lena n-áirítear `<PREFIX>_HOST_NODE` a `delegate_to` sa ról céanna léann. Marker Téann ar nó go díreach os cionn an áirítear `- name:`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a file to contain its own relative path from the repo root as a string literal. Reserved for load-bearing self-references. Repo-root files are exempt without a marker."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn comhad a bhfuil a cosán coibhneasta féin ón fhréamh repo mar teaghrán litriúil. Cúlchiste le haghaidh féintreoracha ualachiompartha. Tá comhaid Repo-fréamh díolmhaithe gan mharcáil."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a hardcoded `http://` / `https://` literal next to a `lookup(...)` call. Reserved for genuinely fixed protocols (Docker-network upstreams, loopback URLs in CI fixtures)."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn cruachódaithe `http://` / Baile `https://` litriúil in aice le `lookup(...)` glaoch. Cúlchiste le haghaidh prótacail atá socraithe go fírinneach (Docker-network upstreams, URLanna ais i daingneáin CI)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a lookup plugin (`plugins/lookup/` or `roles/*/lookup_plugins/`) to import a config-merge function from `utils.cache.applications` / `.domains` / `.users` instead of reaching the SPOT via `lookup_loader.get('applications'/'config'/'domains'/'users')`. Reserved for the SPOT providers (`applications` / `config` / `applications_current_play` / `users` / `domains`) and the raw-volume accessors (`volume` / `nginx`)."
msgstr "Ceadaigh breiseán Lookup (`plugins/lookup/` nó `roles/*/lookup_plugins/`) a allmhairiú fheidhm config-cumasc ó `utils.cache.applications` / Baile `.domains` / Baile `.users` in ionad a bhaint amach ar an mbreac via `lookup_loader.get('applications'/'config'/'domains'/'users')`. Ar fáil do na soláthraithe pacáistithe (`applications` / Baile `config` / Baile `applications_current_play` / Baile `users` / Baile `domains`) agus na rochtaineoirí amh-toirte (`volume` / Baile `nginx`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `Path.read_text` / `Path.read_bytes` call in `tests/lint/` outside the LRU-cached `utils.cache.files.read_text` contract."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn amh `Path.read_text` / Baile `Path.read_bytes` glaoch ar `tests/lint/` taobh amuigh den LRU-cached `utils.cache.files.read_text` conradh."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `Path.rglob`, `os.walk`, or `glob.glob` call outside the `utils.cache.files.iter_project_files` contract."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn amh `Path.rglob`, `os.walk`, nó `glob.glob` glaoch taobh amuigh den `utils.cache.files.iter_project_files` conradh."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `container_name:` key in a `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` template. Default path: route through the generic `compose_only` lookup (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'container_name', NAME) }}`) so swarm-mode replicas do not collide on the static name."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn amh `container_name:` eochair i `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` teimpléad. cosán réamhshocraithe: bealach tríd an gcineálach `compose_only` taiseachas aeir: fliuch (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'container_name', NAME) }}`) mar sin nach bhfuil macasamhla swarm-mode collide ar an ainm statach."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `pull_policy:` key in a `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` template. Default path: route through the generic `compose_only` lookup (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'pull_policy', 'never') }}`) so swarm does not reject the compose-only extension with \"Additional property pull_policy is not allowed\"."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn amh `pull_policy:` eochair i `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` teimpléad. cosán réamhshocraithe: bealach tríd an gcineálach `compose_only` taiseachas aeir: fliuch (`{{ lookup('compose_only', 'pull_policy', 'never') }}`) mar sin ní dhéanann swarm diúltú an leathnú-amháinte le \"Maoin bhreise pull_policy nach bhfuil ceadaithe\"."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a raw `restart:` key in a `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` template. Default path: route through the `compose_restart` lookup so swarm-mode does not silently drop the operator's `docker_restart_policy`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn amh `restart:` eochair i `roles/*/templates/**/*.j2` teimpléad. cosán réamhshocraithe: bealach tríd an `compose_restart` lookup sin ní swarm-mode titim go ciúin an t-oibreoir `docker_restart_policy`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a role task to render a `*.service.j2` itself instead of handing the unit to `sys-service`. Default path: name the template `templates/systemctl.service.j2` and include `sys-service` with `system_service_id`, so the unit also gets the daemon reload, the enable, and the timer, async and flush behaviour. Reserved for units `sys-service` cannot carry, such as a user-scope unit under `$HOME`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn tasc ról a dhéanamh `*.service.j2` féin in ionad an t-aonad a thabhairt ar láimh chun `sys-service`. cosán réamhshocraithe: ainm an teimpléad `templates/systemctl.service.j2` agus san áireamh `sys-service` le `system_service_id`, mar sin faigheann an t-aonad an t-athlódáil daemon, an cumas, agus an t-amadóir, async agus iompar dúiseacht. Cúltaca d'aonaid `sys-service` Ní féidir a iompar, mar aonad úsáideora-scóip faoi `$HOME`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a rule in a `roles/*/templates/nftables.conf.j2` fragment to end in an `accept` verdict. Default path: express the intent as a `drop` of what must not pass, or put the rule in the chain carrying the policy it has to overrule, because an `accept` terminates only its own base chain and every other chain at that hook still runs, docker's `drop` policy on forwarded packets included. Reserved for an accept whose only job is to skip the fragment's own later rules."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn riail i `roles/*/templates/nftables.conf.j2` il go deireadh i `accept` fíorasc. cosán réamhshocraithe: in iúl an intinn mar `drop` de cad nach mór pas a fháil, nó a chur ar an riail sa slabhra ag iompar an pholasaí tá sé a overrule, mar gheall ar `accept` foirceannadh ach a slabhra bonn féin agus gach slabhra eile ag an Hook ritheann fós, docker ar `drop` beartas ar phaicéid ar aghaidh san áireamh. Cúlchiste le haghaidh glacadh a bhfuil ach post a skip na ilroinnte rialacha féin ina dhiaidh sin."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows a single `when:` item to reference a `run_once_<other>` flag whose suffix differs from the current role."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn amháin `when:` mír chun tagairt a dhéanamh `run_once_<other>` bratach a bhfuil difríocht idir a iarmhír ón ról reatha."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows advanced content filtering (e.g., via Lua body/headers)"
msgstr "Allows ábhar chun cinn scagadh (e.g., trí chomhlacht Lua / headers)"

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows an image reference whose tag names a Debian release by codename. Reserved for an upstream that publishes no numeric tag; the marker MUST name which upstream, because a codename pin can never be raised by the updater."
msgstr "Ceadaigh tagairt íomhá a bhfuil a n-ainmneacha tag scaoileadh Debian ag codename. Cúlchiste le haghaidh sruthanna a fhoilsíonn aon chlib uimhriúil; an marcóir MUST ainm a upstream, toisc nach féidir le bioráin códainm a ardú riamh ag an updater."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows an untyped `container inspect` under `roles/`. Default path: pin `--type container`, because a role's overlay network carries the same entity name as its main container, so an untyped inspect can resolve the network and report `map has no entry for key \"State\"`. Use the typed subcommand (`container volume inspect` etc.) when the target genuinely is not a container."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn an untyped `container inspect` faoi bhun `roles/`. cosán réamhshocraithe: bioráin `--type container`, toisc go ndéanann líonra overlay ról an t-ainm eintiteas céanna mar a coimeádán is mó, mar sin is féidir iniúchadh untyped réiteach ar an líonra agus tuarascáil `map has no entry for key \"State\"`. Bain úsáid as an subcommand clóscríofa (`container volume inspect` etc.) nuair nach bhfuil an sprioc fíor coimeádán."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows contributors on Windows to run the full local stack without a separate VM"
msgstr "Ceadaíonn rannchuiditheoirí ar Windows a reáchtáil ar an Stack áitiúil iomlán gan VM ar leith"

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows forced execution during maintenance runs (`MODE_CLEANUP`)."
msgstr "Ceadaigh fhorghníomhú iallach le linn ritheann cothabháil (`MODE_CLEANUP`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows forced execution during maintenance runs (``MODE_CLEANUP``)."
msgstr "Ceadaigh fhorghníomhú iallach le linn ritheann cothabháil (``MODE_CLEANUP``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows instant, low-latency bidirectional traffic"
msgstr "Ceadaíonn tráchta déthreoch toirt, íseal-latency"

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows the agent to resolve unknown APIs and tooling questions without leaving the terminal."
msgstr "Ligeann an gníomhaire a réiteach APIs anaithnid agus ceisteanna tooling gan fágáil an críochfort."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows the marked `ARG` to carry a default. The caller normally supplies every build argument so a missing one fails the build instead of selecting a base image nobody chose."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn an marcáilte `ARG` chun mainneachtain a dhéanamh. An glaoiteoir soláthairtí de ghnáth gach argóint a thógáil mar sin theipeann ar cheann ar iarraidh an tógáil in ionad a roghnú íomhá bonn roghnaigh aon duine."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows the marked `yaml.safe_load` / `safe_dump` call to bypass `utils.cache.yaml`. MUST use `nocheck:`, not `noqa:`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn an marcáilte `yaml.safe_load` / Baile `safe_dump` glaoch ar sheachbhóthar `utils.cache.yaml`. Úsáid MUST `nocheck:`, Níl, `noqa:`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows the marked task to carry a credential without `no_log` on itself or a parent. Marker goes on or directly above the task's `- name:`."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn an tasc marcáilte a sheoladh dintiúir gan `no_log` ar féin nó tuismitheoir. Marker Téann ar nó go díreach os cionn an tasc `- name:`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows the redundant `| bool | ternary('true','false')` pattern when a consumer requires the lowercase tokens."
msgstr "Ceadaítear an iomarcaíocht `| bool | ternary('true','false')` patrún nuair a éilíonn an tomhaltóir na comharthaí níos ísle."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows traffic from the WireGuard client interface (e.g. `wg0-client`) and sets up NAT masquerading on the external interface (e.g. `eth0`)."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn trácht ón gcomhéadan cliant WireGuard (e.g. `wg0-client`) agus leagann suas masquerading NAT ar an gcomhéadan seachtrach (e.g. `eth0`)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Allows traffic from the WireGuard client interface (e.g. ``wg0-client``) and sets up NAT masquerading on the external interface (e.g. ``eth0``)."
msgstr "Ceadaíonn trácht ón gcomhéadan cliant WireGuard (e.g.``wg0-client``) agus leagann suas masquerading NAT ar an gcomhéadan seachtrach (e.g.``eth0``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Alpine Linux → ``openssh-client``"
msgstr "Alpach Linux → ``openssh-client``"

# libretranslate
msgid "Alpine Linux → `openssh-client`"
msgstr "Alpach Linux → `openssh-client`"

# libretranslate
msgid "Already wired via an infinito-native service flag in the row role's `meta/services.yml` (group-gated). Links to that declaration."
msgstr "sreangaithe cheana féin trí bhratach seirbhíse infinito-native i ról an tsraith `meta/services.yml` (grúpa-gated). Naisc leis an dearbhú sin."

# libretranslate
msgid "Also callable directly from Python (unit tests, helpers) without a Jinja context: in that case the only positional argument is the value and compose-style quoting is used."
msgstr "Chomh maith leis sin inghlaoite go díreach ó Python (tástálacha aonaid, cúntóirí) gan comhthéacs Jinja: sa chás sin is é an t-aon argóint suite an luach agus comhdhéanadh-stíl luaite a úsáidtear."

# libretranslate
msgid "Also manually dispatchable: `cron-images-mirror-all.yml`, `cron-images-cleanup-ci.yml`, `cron-cleanup-stale.yml`, `cron-update.yml`, `cron-release-highest.yml`, `call-release-version.yml`, `call-lint.yml`, `call-test.yml`, `call-test-dns.yml`, `call-test-workspace.yml`, `call-test-runner-smoke.yml`."
msgstr "Chomh maith leis sin de láimh dispatchable: `cron-images-mirror-all.yml`, `cron-images-cleanup-ci.yml`, `cron-cleanup-stale.yml`, `cron-update.yml`, `cron-release-highest.yml`, `call-release-version.yml`, `call-lint.yml`, `call-test.yml`, `call-test-dns.yml`, `call-test-workspace.yml`, `call-test-runner-smoke.yml`."

