# libretranslate
msgid "Anything else gets `return 404`, and finding that out was worth the deploy. With `mcp.enabled` false, Baserow's canonical vhost still answered `401 Endpoint not found.` on `/mcp/<key>/sse`, because the image mounts the MCP app on the ASGI root unconditionally and the flag only governs whether an endpoint record is provisioned. A refused credential is still a surface, which is what the disabled-state assertion says and why it failed. The same routing has a sharper edge while MCP is *on*: the adapter narrows fourteen upstream tools to four, and a publicly routed native path walks straight past it to all fourteen for anyone holding the endpoint key. `web-app-homeassistant` had the same shape, an `exposure: internal` surface reachable on its public vhost. Both now 404 there and stay reachable on the container network, which is what `internal` was always supposed to mean."
msgstr "Rud ar bith faigheann `return 404`, agus a aimsiú go raibh amach fiú an imscaradh. Le haghaidh `mcp.enabled` bréagach, d'fhreagair vhost Canonical Baserow fós `401 Endpoint not found.` ar aghaidh `/mcp/<key>/sse`, toisc go mounts an íomhá an app MCP ar an fhréamh ASGI gan choinníoll agus rialaíonn an bhratach ach an bhfuil taifead endpoint ar fáil. Tá dintiúir diúltaithe fós dromchla, a bhfuil an méid a deir an dearbhú faoi mhíchumas-stáit agus cén fáth gur theip air. Tá imeall níos géire ag an ródú céanna agus tá MCP *ar aghaidh*: cúngaíonn an adapter ceithre uirlisí réamhtheachtach déag go ceithre, agus siúlóidí cosán dúchais ród go poiblí díreach anuas go dtí gach ceithre cinn déag do dhuine ar bith a bhfuil an eochair endpoint. `web-app-homeassistant` Bhí an cruth céanna, ar `exposure: internal` dromchla reachable ar a vhost poiblí. An dá anois 404 ann agus fanacht reachable ar an líonra coimeádán, a bhfuil an méid `internal` Bhí ceaptha i gcónaí a chiallaíonn."

# libretranslate
