msgid "Both fields used to live nested inside `meta/main.yml.galaxy_info`:"
msgstr "An dá réimsí a úsáidtear chun cónaí neadaithe taobh istigh `meta/main.yml.galaxy_info`:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both halves are required: ``tor.enabled`` is the dependency edge, not the port forward, so a client picking the Tor transport from that flag alone dials a port with no HiddenServicePort and no host publish."
msgstr "Tá an dá leath ag teastáil: ``tor.enabled`` Is é an imeall dependency, nach bhfuil an calafort ar aghaidh, mar sin le cliant ag piocadh an t-iompar Tor as an bhratach sin amháin dials port gan aon HiddenServicePort agus gan aon óstach a fhoilsiú."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both helpers degrade gracefully:"
msgstr "An dá Cúntóirí degrade gracefully:"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``, which targets the ``openid-connect/auth`` href explicitly, opens ``/admin``, and signs out at ``/admin/ui/logout``; a second scenario drives the biber-to-administrator mail round-trip across two browser contexts. The path back to the generic personas is a distinguishable login control on Mailu’s SSO page."
msgstr "Tá an dá thuras clúdaithe bespoke i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``, a dhíríonn ar an ``openid-connect/auth`` href sainráite, osclaíonn ``/admin``, agus comharthaí amach ag ``/admin/ui/logout``; thiomáineann an dara cás an biber-le-administrator phost bhabhta-turas trasna dhá chomhthéacs bhrabhsálaí. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach rialú logáil isteach ar leathanach SSO Mailu ar."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: the master-realm super administrator drives the admin console, and the normal-realm administrator and biber each drive the realm account console including sign-out. The path back to the generic personas is an app-shaped surface behind the shared auth chain, which the identity provider by definition does not have."
msgstr "Tá an dá thuras clúdaithe bespoke i ``files/playwright/playwright.spec.js``: thiomáineann an máistir-realm riarthóir Super an consól admin, agus an riarthóir gnáth-realm agus biber gach tiomáint an consól cuntas realm lena n-áirítear comhartha-amach. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach dromchla app-chruthach taobh thiar den slabhra auth roinnte, nach bhfuil an soláthraí aitheantais de réir sainmhíniú."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, which targets the `openid-connect/auth` href explicitly, opens `/admin`, and signs out at `/admin/ui/logout`; a second scenario drives the biber-to-administrator mail round-trip across two browser contexts. The path back to the generic personas is a distinguishable login control on Mailu's SSO page."
msgstr "Tá an dá thuras clúdaithe bespoke i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`, a dhíríonn ar an `openid-connect/auth` href sainráite, osclaíonn `/admin`, agus comharthaí amach ag `/admin/ui/logout`; thiomáineann an dara cás an biber-le-administrator phost bhabhta-turas trasna dhá chomhthéacs bhrabhsálaí. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach rialú logáil isteach ar leathanach SSO Mailu ar."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both journeys are covered bespoke in `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: the master-realm super administrator drives the admin console, and the normal-realm administrator and biber each drive the realm account console including sign-out. The path back to the generic personas is an app-shaped surface behind the shared auth chain, which the identity provider by definition does not have."
msgstr "Tá an dá thuras clúdaithe bespoke i `files/playwright/playwright.spec.js`: thiomáineann an máistir-realm riarthóir Super an consól admin, agus an riarthóir gnáth-realm agus biber gach tiomáint an consól cuntas realm lena n-áirítear comhartha-amach. Is é an cosán ar ais go dtí an personas cineálach dromchla app-chruthach taobh thiar den slabhra auth roinnte, nach bhfuil an soláthraí aitheantais de réir sainmhíniú."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both layers are process-wide in-process caches. They intentionally do NOT track on-disk file mtimes; CLI tools are short-lived and the assumption \"the on-disk file does not change while my process runs\" holds. The single exception is `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, which writes through and evicts the cached entry for the path it just wrote so a tool that edits a file mid-run sees the new content on the next read."
msgstr "Tá an dá shraith ar fud an phróisis i-próiseálaí. Déanann siad d'aon ghnó NACH rian ar mtimes comhad; Tá uirlisí CLI gearr-cónaí agus an toimhde \"nach bhfuil an comhad ar-díosca athrú cé go ritheann mo phróiseas\" seilbh. Is é an eisceacht amháin `utils.cache.yaml.dump_yaml`, a scríobhann tríd agus evicts an iontráil i dtaisce don cosán scríobh sé díreach mar sin uirlis a in eagar comhad lár-reáchtáil Feiceann an t-ábhar nua ar an chéad léamh eile."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both need the same facts about a role: whether it ships its own container stack, and which deploy modes it supports. Keeping the logic here means the two callers never drift."
msgstr "Ní mór an dá na fíricí céanna faoi ról: cibé an long sé a chairn coimeádán féin, agus a modhanna imscaradh tacaíonn sé. Ciallaíonn a choinneáil ar an loighic anseo an dá callers riamh sruth."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both on the position"
msgstr "An dá ar an seasamh"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both paths elevate privileges via `sudo` when not run as root, and the script verifies `bwrap` and `socat` on `PATH` before it exits. macOS uses `sandbox-exec` from the base system and does not need this target."
msgstr "An dá cosáin pribhléidí elevate trí `sudo` nuair nach reáchtáil mar fhréamh, agus fíoraíonn an script `bwrap` agus `socat` ar aghaidh `PATH` sula bhfágann sé. úsáidí macOS `sandbox-exec` ón gcóras bonn agus ní gá an sprioc seo."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both platforms run model-generated code, which is untrusted, so a kernel-level boundary is required on top of their in-app sandboxing. [gVisor](https://gvisor.dev/) provides that boundary behind an OCI runtime, so each agent app stays a normal container spec and only pins `runtime: runsc`, reusing the existing image pipeline, replicas, healthchecks, and dual-mode machinery. [Kata Containers](https://katacontainers.io/) wrapping Firecracker was the original choice; Decision #2 records why it is unreachable on this container engine. ([E2B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) is the higher-level alternative but brings its own Nomad/Consul orchestration and x86-cloud self-host, which would replace the swarm model.)"
msgstr "An dá ardáin reáchtáil cód samhail-generated, a bhfuil untrusted, mar sin tá teorainn ar leibhéal eithne ag teastáil ar bharr a n-in-app sandboxing. [taiseachas aeir: fliuch](https://gvisor.dev/) Soláthraíonn go teorainn taobh thiar de runtime OCI, mar sin fanann gach app gníomhaire spec coimeádán gnáth agus bioráin amháin `runtime: runsc`, athúsáid a bhaint as an bpíblíne íomhá atá ann cheana féin, macasamhail, healthchecks, agus dé-mode innealra. [coimeádáin Kata](https://katacontainers.io/) Bhí timfhilleadh Firecracker an rogha bunaidh; Cinneadh #2 taifid cén fáth go bhfuil sé unreachable ar an inneall coimeádán. ([E2B B B B](https://github.com/e2b-dev/infra) Is é an rogha eile leibhéal níos airde ach tugann sé a ceolfhoirne féin Nomad / Consul agus x86-cloud féin-óstach, a bheadh in ionad an tsamhail swarm.)"

# libretranslate
msgid "Both pools feed the assignment, so narrowing `distros` to one value pins every row to it rather than reducing the run."
msgstr "An dá linnte beatha an sannadh, chomh caolú `distros` le bioráin luach amháin gach sraith dó seachas an rith a laghdú."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both renderers fail loudly when Jinja markers cannot be resolved so generated configs never silently leak unrendered placeholders."
msgstr "Theipeann ar an dá rindreálaithe os ard nuair nach féidir le marcóirí Jinja a réiteach chomh configs a ghintear riamh leak gan staonadh sealbhóirí áite."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both requirement files name the same collections at the same versions: the Galaxy file is the normal source, the git file the fallback used when galaxy.ansible.com is unreachable. A bump that touches only one of them would make the fallback install something the pin does not describe, so an update is applied to both or to neither."
msgstr "An dá comhaid ceanglas ainm na bailiúcháin céanna ag na leaganacha céanna: Is é an comhad Réaltra an fhoinse gnáth, an comhad git an fallback a úsáidtear nuair a galaxy.ansible.com Níl sé indéanta. Bheadh bump go baint ach ceann amháin acu a dhéanamh ar an fallback shuiteáil rud éigin nach bhfuil an bioráin cur síos, mar sin tá nuashonrú i bhfeidhm ar an dá nó nach."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both run from the trusted workflow ref and check out the version tag for the actual build payload, so the release artefacts match the tagged commit byte-for-byte."
msgstr "An dá reáchtáil as an athshocrú sreabhadh oibre iontaofa agus seiceáil amach an chlib leagan don ualach pá a thógáil iarbhír, mar sin na déantáin scaoileadh mheaitseáil leis an clib tiomantas byte-do-byte."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both sides pass `primary_apps` (not the round closure) as the BFS seed and the variant-merged services map for that round, so the reachability walk sees the same topology the inventory baked."
msgstr "An dá thaobh pas `primary_apps` (nach bhfuil an dúnadh bhabhta) mar an síol BFS agus an léarscáil seirbhísí athraitheach le chéile don bhabhta sin, mar sin feiceann an siúlóid sroichte an topology céanna an fardal baked."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both sources carry the same pinned collections, so the only thing separating them is how long they take and whether they answer at all. A single slow day says nothing: galaxy.ansible.com degrades and recovers, and a git clone can stall on one runner. The default is therefore retuned only when a rolling window of daily samples shows one source durably behind the other."
msgstr "Déanann an dá fhoinse na bailiúcháin pinned céanna, mar sin is é an rud amháin a dheighilt iad cé chomh fada a ghlacann siad agus an bhfreagraíonn siad ar chor ar bith. Deir lá mall amháin rud ar bith: galaxy.ansible.com degrades agus recovers, agus is féidir le Clón git stalla ar dara háit amháin. Dá bhrí sin, ní dhéantar an mhainneachtain ach amháin nuair a léiríonn fuinneog rollta na samplaí laethúla foinse amháin go mór taobh thiar den cheann eile."

#, no-python-format
msgid "Both targets (Debian changelog and the RPM ``%changelog`` section) are fully regenerated on every run from the kept entries plus an archived-releases notice that points at the documentation site and lists the archived versions and dates as plain text. The notice is folded into the body of the oldest kept entry (not appended after the last entry), because free text after the final entry is not valid changelog data and makes the native parsers warn. Because the package files are regenerated, they cannot drift from the CHANGELOG.md SPOT."
msgstr ""

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required."
msgstr "An dá théarma (application_id, service_key) ag teastáil."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required. ``services.<service_key>.name`` must exist in the resolved application config."
msgstr "An dá théarma (application_id, service_key) ag teastáil. ``services.<service_key>.name`` ní mór a bheith ann sa choigist iarratais a réiteach."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required. ``services.<service_key>.name`` must exist in the resolved application config; the stack name is derived from ``application_id`` via the ``get_entity_name`` filter (matching how ``docker stack deploy`` names the stack in ``sys-svc-compose/handlers/main.yml``)."
msgstr "An dá théarma (application_id, service_key) ag teastáil. ``services.<service_key>.name`` Ní mór a bheith ann sa config iarratas réiteach; Tá an t-ainm Stack a dhíorthaítear ó ``application_id`` tríd an ``get_entity_name`` scagaire scagaire (meaitseáil conas a ``docker stack deploy`` ainmneacha an chairn i ``sys-svc-compose/handlers/main.yml``)."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both terms (application_id, service_key) are required; they are validated by `image`."
msgstr "An dá théarma (application_id, service_key) ag teastáil; tá siad bailíochtaithe ag `image`."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both tests route every read through the project caches (`utils.cache.files`, `utils.cache.yaml`); contributors adding a new variable scanner MUST do the same instead of calling `yaml.safe_load*` or `open()` directly."
msgstr "An dá tástálacha bealach gach léamh tríd an taisce tionscadail (`utils.cache.files`, `utils.cache.yaml`); rannchuiditheoirí ag cur MUST scanóir athróg nua a dhéanamh mar an gcéanna in ionad glaoch `yaml.safe_load*` nó `open()` go díreach."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both the CLI that parses ``--set`` and the inventory manager that consumes the parsed pairs build the key here, so a credential is addressed by exactly one string. A short form would name different credentials on different apps."
msgstr "An dá CLI go parses ``--set`` agus an bainisteoir fardal a itheann na péirí parsed a thógáil ar an eochair anseo, mar sin tá dintiúir aghaidh ag díreach teaghrán amháin. Bheadh foirm ghearr ainm dintiúir éagsúla ar apps éagsúla."

# libretranslate
msgid "Both the role-meta lint (`tests/lint/ansible/services/test_addons_schema.py`) and the opt-in external drift checker (`tests/external/update/addons/`) read the constants here so the two layers never drift apart: the lint validates that an addon's declared `mechanism`/`source`/`update.catalog` is one the checker actually understands, and the checker only walks catalogs it has an adapter for."
