# libretranslate
msgid "Decision 7's \"proxy + SSO\" is served by `services.sso.flavor: oidc` on `web-app-litellm` plus LiteLLM's own `GENERIC_*` OIDC settings, rendered into the gateway's env behind `LITELLM_UI_SSO`. An oauth2-proxy sidecar is not an option here: `get_entity_name` maps both `web-app-litellm` and `svc-ai-litellm` to `litellm`, so the two roles share one compose directory, one swarm stack name and one docker network name, and a second stack would overwrite the gateway's `compose.yml` and delete its service under `docker stack deploy --prune`. `web-app-bigbluebutton` is the precedent for a stackless role carrying `flavor: oidc`. The trade-off: an anonymous request reaches LiteLLM's own login page rather than being refused at the edge, and LiteLLM caps SSO at five accounts without a licence."
msgstr "Cinneadh an Chinnidh 7's \"seachfhreastalaí + SSO\" a sheirbheáil ag `services.sso.flavor: oidc` ar aghaidh `web-app-litellm` móide LiteLM féin `GENERIC_*` socruithe OIDC, a rinneadh isteach sa tairseach taobh thiar de `LITELLM_UI_SSO`. Níl an Tweet seo ar fáil2-Ní rogha é sidecar stráice anseo: `get_entity_name` léarscáileanna an dá `web-app-litellm` agus `svc-ai-litellm` go dtí `litellm`, mar sin a roinnt ar an dá ról eolaire chumadh amháin, ainm Stack swarm amháin agus ainm líonra docker amháin, agus bheadh an dara Stack scríobh an geata ar `compose.yml` agus a sheirbhís a scriosadh `docker stack deploy --prune`. `web-app-bigbluebutton` Is é an fasach le haghaidh ról stackless iompar `flavor: oidc`. An trádáil-uaire: sroicheann iarratas gan ainm leathanach logála LiteLM féin seachas a dhiúltú ar an imeall, agus caipíní LiteLM SSO ag cúig chuntas gan cheadúnas."

