# libretranslate
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Deploy jobs are matched by the compose/swarm/host glyph (from the symbol glossary, the single source of truth) their test-deploy-{compose,swarm,host}.yml matrix titles them with -- NOT the words \"Compose\"/\"Swarm\"/\"Host\", which no real job carries (matching those made ``--failed swarm`` silently find nothing). What follows the glyph is the role's display name (``utils.roles.display``), decoded back to the role id; a bare role id from a run that predates the display names decodes just as well. The orchestrator prepends a \"caller / \" prefix and the shard suffix (e.g. \" 0,1\") rides along in the display name; both are tolerated."
msgstr "Deploy jobs are matched ag an compose/swarm/host cineál gas: leathadh (as an snasta siombail, an fhoinse amháin na fírinne) a thástáil-deploy-{chumadh, cogadh, óstáil}.yml maitrís teidil iad le - NACH na focail \"Compose\"/ Baile\"Swarm\"/ Baile\"Host\", nach ndéanann aon phost fíor (meaitseáil iad siúd a rinneadh ``--failed swarm`` adh aimsiú rud ar bith). Cad a leanas an glyph Is é an ról ainm taispeáint (``utils.roles.display``), díchódaithe ar ais go dtí an ról id; ról lom id ó reáchtáil go predates an ainmneacha a thaispeáint decodes díreach chomh maith. An ceoltóir prepends a \"glaoiteoir / \" réim agus iarmhír an chúd (e.g. \" 0,1\") rides chomh maith san ainm taispeáint; araon a fhulaingt."

