# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw exposes no administrator-visible list of configured MCP servers, so the configured set is proven by a CLI test instead: [`files/test/test.sh`](./files/test/test.sh) probes the agent's `mcp` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a `failed to start server` line. The Playwright spec covers the complementary case, that the gateway holding the MCP credentials refuses an unauthenticated caller."
msgstr "OpenClaw nochtann aon liosta riarthóir-visible de freastalaithe MCP cumraithe, mar sin tá an sraith cumraithe cruthaithe ag tástáil CLI ionad: [`files/test/test.sh`](./files/test/test.sh) probes an gníomhaire `mcp` dromchla agus go mainneoidh nuair a dhéanann an exec féin nó an t-aschur `failed to start server` líne. Clúdaíonn an spec Playwright an cás comhlántach, go bhfuil an geata a bhfuil na dintiúir MCP diúltaíonn glaoiteoir unauthenticated."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw exposes no administrator-visible list of configured MCP servers, so the configured set is proven by a CLI test instead: ```files/test/test.sh`` <./files/test/test.sh>`__ probes the agent’s ``mcp`` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a ``failed to start server`` line. The Playwright spec covers the complementary case, that the gateway holding the MCP credentials refuses an unauthenticated caller."
msgstr "OpenClaw nochtann aon liosta riarthóir-visible de freastalaithe MCP cumraithe, mar sin tá an sraith cumraithe cruthaithe ag tástáil CLI ionad: ```files/test/test.sh`` <./files/test/test.sh>`__ probes the agent’s ``mcp`` surface and fails when the exec itself fails or the output carries a ``failed to start server`` líne. Clúdaíonn an spec Playwright an cás comhlántach, go bhfuil an geata a bhfuil na dintiúir MCP diúltaíonn glaoiteoir unauthenticated."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenClaw's own CLI reference says so directly: `openclaw mcp serve` \"starts a stdio MCP server\" whose process \"the MCP client owns\". Every HTTP transport in that document belongs to the opposite direction, `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, which is OpenClaw acting as a client. Hermes is the same shape: both entry points, `mcp_serve.py` and `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, run the MCP SDK's stdio transport, the repository defines neither `run_streamable_http_async` nor `sse_app`, and the user-facing MCP guide describes only Hermes consuming external servers."
msgstr "Deir tagairt CLI féin OpenClaw mar sin go díreach: `openclaw mcp serve` \"Tosaíonn freastalaí MCP stdio\" a phróiseas \"úinéireacht an cliant MCP\". Baineann gach iompar HTTP sa doiciméad sin leis an treo eile, `openclaw mcp add --url --transport streamable-http`, atá OpenClaw ag gníomhú mar chliant. Is é Hermes an cruth céanna: an dá phointe iontrála, `mcp_serve.py` agus `agent/transports/hermes_tools_mcp_server.py`, reáchtáil iompar stdio an MCP SDK, Sainmhíníonn an stór nach `run_streamable_http_async` agus ní `sse_app`, agus an t-úsáideoir-facing MCP treoir síos ach Hermes Tógann freastalaithe seachtracha."

