# libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk"
msgstr "Nuacht agus Imeachtaí"

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk authenticates users against the central Keycloak realm via OIDC and looks up users via the Keycloak admin Web API (`keycloak_webapi` backend). OpenLDAP feeds OpenTalk transitively through Keycloak's federation."
msgstr "OpenTalk údar úsáideoirí i gcoinne an réimse lárnach Keycloak via OIDC agus tá sé suas úsáideoirí tríd an API Gréasáin Keycloak admin (`keycloak_webapi` riachtanais uisce: measartha). Fothaí OpenLDAP OpenTalk go huathoibríoch trí chónaidhm Keycloak ar."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk authenticates users via OIDC and resolves invitee searches via `https://<keycloak>/admin/realms/<realm>/users?search=…`."
msgstr "OpenTalk fíordheimhnithe úsáideoirí trí OIDC agus réitíonn cuardaigh cuireadh trí `https://<keycloak>/admin/realms/<realm>/users?search=…`."

# libretranslate
msgid "OpenTalk does not open LDAP connections itself. It relies on Keycloak's LDAP federation (`svc-db-openldap` is mapped into the central Keycloak realm) and queries Keycloak's admin Web API for user lookups. This avoids dual-source-of-truth problems and keeps LDAP credentials away from the OpenTalk service account."
msgstr "Ní OpenTalk oscailt naisc LDAP féin. Braitheann sé ar chónaidhm LDAP Keycloak (`svc-db-openldap` mapáilte isteach i réimse lárnach Keycloak) agus ceisteanna API Gréasáin admin Keycloak do lookups úsáideora. Seachnaíonn sé seo fadhbanna dé-foinse agus coimeádann dintiúir LDAP ar shiúl ón gcuntas seirbhíse OpenTalk."

# libretranslate
msgid "Opening an adapter provider's network to its clients collides with the sidecar isolation invariant, so one of the two has to give. A provider that declares the `mcp_client` overlay puts its own containers on it: `homeassistant` joins `[homeassistant, homeassistant_default]`. The same declaration on an adapter provider would give its sidecar a second interface, and [`isolation.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/isolation.sh) rejects anything but exactly one, because a sidecar holding the provider's credential must reach that provider only. Today `prometheusmcp` satisfies it with a single attachment and is therefore reachable by no client at all. Either the sidecar joins only the pair network and the provider joins it too, or the isolation check becomes an identity check over the admitted peers rather than a count."
msgstr "Oscail líonra soláthraí adapter ar a chliaint collides leis an invariant leithlisiú sidecar, mar sin tá ar cheann de na dhá a thabhairt. Soláthraí a dhearbhaíonn na `mcp_client` cuireann overlay a choimeádáin féin air: `homeassistant` Uirlisí ilchuspóireacha `[homeassistant, homeassistant_default]`. Bheadh an dearbhú céanna ar sholáthraí adapter a thabhairt ar a sidecar dara comhéadan, agus [`isolation.sh`](../../roles/test-e2e-cli/files/shared/mcp/isolation.sh) Diúltaíonn rud ar bith ach amháin go díreach, mar ní mór do sidecar a bhfuil dintiúir an tsoláthraí teacht ar an soláthraí sin amháin. Sa lá atá inniu ann `prometheusmcp` sásaíonn sé le ceangaltán amháin agus dá bhrí sin is reachable ag aon chliant ar chor ar bith. Ceachtar an sidecar théann ach an líonra péire agus an soláthraí a théann sé freisin, nó an tseiceáil leithlisiú thiocfaidh chun bheith ina seiceáil aitheantais thar na piaraí a ligean isteach seachas comhaireamh."

# libretranslate
msgid "Opening the PR through a GitHub App installation token bypasses this restriction. The App counts as a distinct actor, so PR-lifecycle events fire normally and the full CI pipeline runs against every update PR."
msgstr "Oscailt an PR trí shuiteáil GitHub App sheachbhóthar an srian. An App chomhaireamh mar aisteoir ar leith, mar sin imeachtaí PR-saoil dóiteáin de ghnáth agus ritheann an píblíne CI iomlán i gcoinne gach nuashonrú PR."

